{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me","id":610887,"title":"Beat the heroism of the Garou back into me.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-01T08:40:24-07:00","id":610887,"title":"Beat the heroism of the Garou back into me.","content":"I knew some ... jerk for a while who tried brainwashing me into thinking the garou arent heros.<br /> <br /> That environmentalism is garbage and some other bullshit.<br /> <br /> I submit myself for deprogramming","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T10:03:35-07:00","id":610990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me#post610887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I knew some ... jerk for a while who tried brainwashing me into thinking the garou arent heros.<br /> <br /> That environmentalism is garbage and some other bullshit.<br /> <br /> I submit myself for deprogramming</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh... might need a little more to go on than that. Have you re-read the books? Someone who doesn't have a good handle on Werewolf might sit there and come up with a lot of strawman arguments about why the Garou suck.<br /> <br /> However, Garou are some of the most heroic creatures in the oWoD. They are incredibly violent and far from perfect, but they war against an entropic force that threatens all of creation. They are flawed things, but by and large, the Nation strives to do what is best for Gaia, at great personal cost. Teleologically speaking, that is pretty good and heroic. <br /> <br /> If you are saying that killing people or monsters over environmental themes is bad or stupid, that might just be personal taste. It can take a lot of creativity to present such themes as interesting or fresh. Corrupt humans and evil spirits are literally killing the soul of the planet, alright, I get it... but for that to matter, for that to have emotional impact for the players, environmental catastrophes have to <i>be visceral, they have to hurt or disgust.</i> Oil spattered ducks are one thing, but your wife and kids wasting away due to poisoning by heavy metals might carry a bit more weight...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T11:32:09-07:00","id":611102,"title":"","content":":A summary of her bullshit<br /> <br /> The garou are not sentient because their behaviour is controlled by a dice roller<br /> <br /> Their unnatural, because of their supernatural abilitys and the fact they cannot create healthy offspring with their own kind<br /> <br /> A bunch of bullshit about how Dogs have a definite evolutioinary advantage over wolves , how tool use IS an evolutionary advantage, and a bunch of other garbage.<br /> <br /> oh some insanity about how environmentalism is the product of people who are not struggling to survive, and often considered gross hypocricy by those who are.<br /> <br /> ANOTHER peice of bullshit she had, was that lupus should be athiestic, since animals dont have religion....<br /> <br /> Oh an argument that Garou are INFERIOR to humanity that I found really really sick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 08-01-2015, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T12:45:49-07:00","id":611220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=611102#post611102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">:A summary of her bullshit<br /> <br /> The garou are not sentient because their behaviour is controlled by a dice roller<br /> <br /> Their unnatural, because of their supernatural abilitys and the fact they cannot create healthy offspring with their own kind<br /> <br /> A bunch of bullshit about how Dogs have a definite evolutioinary advantage over wolves , how tool use IS an evolutionary advantage, and a bunch of other garbage.<br /> <br /> oh some insanity about how environmentalism is the product of people who are not struggling to survive, and often considered gross hypocricy by those who are.<br /> <br /> ANOTHER peice of bullshit she had, was that lupus should be athiestic, since animals dont have religion....<br /> <br /> Oh an argument that Garou are INFERIOR to humanity that I found really really sick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have to talk with her very often? Or is she someone that you can avoid? And will explanations and talking actually work, or does she just have an axe to grind?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T12:52:57-07:00","id":611248,"title":"","content":"I Found myself talking with her a lot on AOL Now shes disappeared after over a decade why im begging people to help cure me now.<br /> <br /> I think shes just got a case of blatant intellectualism. she likes showing off how &quot;Friendly and reasonable&quot; she is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T13:50:23-07:00","id":611286,"title":"","content":"They aren't furry superheroes. Garou are more of a tragic figure in the WoD. They are dealing with the repercussions of the actions of their ancestors as they struggle with their own Rage to view others as more than targets to be slaughtered. They struggle with natures of duality where they can never truly fit in to one world or the other but they are forbidden from finding comfort with the only others who could understand them completely. They are a people who are dying out while trying to protect a fundamentally flawed world and sacrifice themselves constantly for no thanks or recognition from anyone other than their own people. They try to save the world for the world's sake and less so for the sake of humanity, i.e. the loss of human life is less important than protecting creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T15:26:43-07:00","id":611407,"title":"","content":"Just my opinions, and you probably won't like some of them. That's fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=611102#post611102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The garou are not sentient because their behaviour is controlled by a dice roller</div> </div> </div> </div>This doesn't make any sense at all. Is she even familiar with roleplaying games?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Their unnatural, because of their supernatural abilitys and the fact they cannot create healthy offspring with their own kind </div> </div> </div>Yes and no, but totally unrelevant. They are natural in the sense that they are part of &quot;Gaia's order&quot;. However, they aren't meant to be separate from humanity or wolves. They are meant to be bridges between them. Gaia did not want them to be separate from humanity or the wolves so she made sure the Changing Breeds can't be insular and reproduce by themselves.<br /> <br /> They are magical beings. Whether that is &quot;natural&quot; or &quot;unnatural&quot; depends on the settings of your fictional world. In the World of Darkness, this doesn't mark it as inherently unnatural.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A bunch of bullshit about how Dogs have a definite evolutioinary advantage over wolves , how tool use IS an evolutionary advantage, and a bunch of other garbage. </div> </div> </div>Strange ideas about dogs. However, tool use is definitely an advantage to humanity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> oh some insanity about how environmentalism is the product of people who are not struggling to survive, and often considered gross hypocricy by those who are. </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say environmentalism itself is weird. There are very good reasons humans want clean air, drinkable water, and other benefits that environmentalism has provided.<br /> <br /> At the same time, there is definitely a romantic view of the wilderness that some environmentalists have that does not fit actual reality. Those are people who are extremely hostile towards modern day civilization and think it would be a good thing to de-industrialize, eliminate advanced farming techniques, and basically return to primitive technology. They don't care about high infant mortality rates, extreme poverty, constant warfare, and the other disadvantages primitive peoples face because it never seems to occur to them. The wilderness (aka Mother Nature) is DANGEROUS. Natural disasters, famines, diseases, and such are just as part of nature as clean air. So I do think your friend has a point - some environmentalists (not all) have a naive and ignorant view of nature.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ANOTHER peice of bullshit she had, was that lupus should be athiestic, since animals dont have religion.... </div> </div> </div>This makes no sense. Animals have no religion, but lupus Garou are not animals. They are Garou born of wolves who know spirits exist and are real, and have an intrinsic tie to them (as their high initial Gnosis indicates)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh an argument that Garou are INFERIOR to humanity that I found really really sick. </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say Garou are inferior, but they are monsters and they do many inhuman, monstrous things from a human perspective (as well as heroic, good things). I think the game benefits from acknowledging both aspects.<br /> <br /> I've never bought into the Captain Planet aspects of the game. Environmental themes are appropriate given the Garou religion and setting, but I don't think it should dominate the game. It crowds out a lot of other elements. Dominating specific chronicles makes sense, but there are also many kinds of chronicles to tell where the environmental aspects are in the background. Certainly, the further back in time you go (if you want to do a historical chronicle), the environmental aspects becomes less important. For most of the thousands of years of Garou history, an environmental theme wouldn't make sense.<br /> <br /> So while the Garou are heroes in an Epic sense along the lines of the Iliad, the myths of Hercules, the Song of Roland, and others, they aren't heroic from a human perspective. Individuals could be, but plenty of Garou heroes would not be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 08-02-2015, 02:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T15:38:35-07:00","id":611419,"title":"","content":"It doesn't take a very deep reading to realize that the Garou are guilty of most of the stuff they accuse humans of, but at the end of the day these hypocritical fuzzy nutjobs are trying to save the world and they <i>are</i> pretty much it's best hope. Which is more or less the entire reason it's so fucked to begin with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T16:04:27-07:00","id":611429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=611407#post611407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This doesn't make any sense at all. Is she even familiar with roleplaying games?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd also add &quot;definitions of words&quot; onto that, seeing as how sentient, in an ethical sense, means the capacity to feel pain or discomfort.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've never bought into the Captain Planet aspects of the game. Environmental themes are appropriate given the Garou religion and setting, but I don't think it should dominate the game. It crowds out a lot of other elements. Dominating specific chronicles makes sense, but there are also many kinds of chronicles to tell where the environmental aspects are in the background. Certainly, the further back in time you go (if you want to do a historical chronicle), the environmental aspects becomes less important. For most of the thousands of years of Garou history, an environmental theme wouldn't make sense. </div> </div> </div>Kind of a tangent, but the vast majority of things that come up in Captain Planet and how they're handled remind me of Mage. Especially when they start going off the rails and adding in shrink rays, time travel, exchanging some abstract &quot;mind&quot; between two bodies, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T00:03:22-07:00","id":611944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=611102#post611102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">:A summary of her bullshit</div> </div> </div> </div>As Black Fox did, I will just tackle the specific topics. But first, I advise you to reevaluate both your friendship and your love for the game. I'm no one to say what kind of thing you have to believe, and maybe she's hurting you in other ways, but seriously, she's a real person, this is just a game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The garou are not sentient because their behaviour is controlled by a dice roller</div> </div> </div> </div>Nonsense. They aren't truly sentient because they're fictional, but in the fiction they are as sentient as anyone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their unnatural, because of their supernatural abilitys and the fact they cannot create healthy offspring with their own kind</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on your definition of natural to begin with, and in the setting it is pretty clear they are considered natural. And just looking to real life biology I can atest the offspring part is pure nonsense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A bunch of bullshit about how Dogs have a definite evolutioinary advantage over wolves , how tool use IS an evolutionary advantage, and a bunch of other garbage.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are no such a thing as definite evolutionary advantages, because evolution doesn't work this way. In fact dogs are in a better position now than wolves, but that doesn't mean something definite, much less the underlying notion of superiority she seems to mean. But this isn't even relevant, in any way. In-setting what's in question is link to the Wyld, and dogs don't have as much, and werewolves aren't wolves, they are themselfs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh some insanity about how environmentalism is the product of people who are not struggling to survive, and often considered gross hypocricy by those who are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Common argument, and a serious one, but here isn't the place to talk about it at length. I would recomend you to search the theme on the web, look for scientific material and draw your own conclusions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">ANOTHER peice of bullshit she had, was that lupus should be athiestic, since animals dont have religion....</div> </div> </div> </div>Just wrong because Lupus aren't wolves, they're Garou. Tha makes a lot of difference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh an argument that Garou are INFERIOR to humanity that I found really really sick</div> </div> </div> </div>Without the proper argument I can't tackle it.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't simply say Garou are heroes because this is the World of Darkness, and the concept of Shades of Grey is pretty important to the setting. But bring her arguments, you clearly needs to talk, and we need them to counter effectively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T19:46:18-07:00","id":612913,"title":"","content":"Dogs are evolutionary advantages over wolves? Please point out to this person that many breeds of pure breed dogs at this point have been so mutated that they have severe health issues. Some breeds are incapable of natural breeding. A dog's main advantage is that men do not hunt them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T20:41:32-07:00","id":612968,"title":"","content":"It doesn't sound like you need much re-programming because you realize that she was bat-shit-crazy, didn't have a real clue about the game, and apparently only read the game with the intent to argue against it like a conspiracy-nut (like the guy who has &quot;proof&quot; that Stephen King killed John Lennon through a government code placed in public magazines...)<br /> <br /> If her argument was simply &quot;Garou are not the heroes they think that they are in the World of Darkness&quot;, we could have a rational discussion regarding that standpoint, both from their way of seeing things, from the Fera, and from an outsider's view.<br /> <br /> However, she's arguing nonsense about the game mechanics, doesn't understand what a Lupus is, and so on.<br /> <br /> So, let's start with a few of the ideas you've brought up:<br /> <br /> <b><u>Garou are Heroic:</u></b><br /> In the World of Darkness, there are very few beings that are trying to save the world. Most are selfish, trying to fight for their own survival or advancement to live forever, or ascend. Only the Hunters (as a fat-splat) could be seen as being more heroic, putting their lives on the line to save the world from the monsters they perceive to be the world's demons.<br /> The Garou believe that they are the only faction that is actively fighting to keep the world from being destroyed by two of the primordial forces of the world (The Wyrm and the Weaver.) They were created to fight the Wyrm and are learning that they must also be aware of the Weaver's power and influence as well.<br /> They are TOO steeped in tradition and connection with their ancestors and spirits to change their ways very quickly. They are fueled by Rage and their own power at times and have done some really tragic and stupid stuff (killing off their Fera allies and making enemies of the survivors, Allowing 1 Tribe to be turned to the Wyrm, and being responsible for the destruction of the Bunyip because they didn't understand them and were tricked by the Wyrm into doing so.) They have been so blinded by the Wyrm that they ignored the rise of the Weaver as a nearly equal adversary. They also are so self-righteous and again so blinded by their traditions and mis-trust that they war among themselves over territory, meanings of their purposes, and the correct paths to take that they've also slaughtered their own kind to be &quot;right&quot;.<br /> Yet, for all of these issues, their unified purpose is to put their lives on the line to fight a war that will hold off the destruction of the world that has been foretold and guaranteed.<br /> <br /> <b><u>The garou are not sentient because their behaviour is controlled by a dice roller:</u></b><br /> Again, this doesn't make much sense, unless it was just how she meant to say that &quot;They are influenced by their Rage, and can Frenzy.&quot; Otherwise, it really doesn't seem like she understood character creation, or the mechanics of the game if she thought that a character's actions were determined by their rolls.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Their unnatural, because of their supernatural abilitys and the fact they cannot create healthy offspring with their own kind</u></b><br /> This sounds like an argument made by hunters (and not Hunters, who are imbued with supernatural powers to fight the rest of the WoD too.)<br /> In the setting and story of Werewolf: the Apocalypse, they are entirely &quot;natural&quot; because the primal forces of the world that decided what were &quot;natural&quot; created them to do what they do.<br /> The fact that they create Metis when breeding with one another is one of those &quot;rules&quot; that the forces that created them determined, and thus that's just part of their natural ways.<br /> We're not talking about designer-mutts here like Doodles, who can't be bred together or else they become genetically muddy. Think of it more as the True Born gene is recessive and when the True Born Garou gets the right genes and becomes True Born, their genetics require more diversity. There are plenty of real-life genetics where two people with recessive genes have a child that is deformed and that's perfectly &quot;natural&quot;, even though it's not optimal (a friend's parents both had a recessive gene that their children would have a 1-in-4 chance of being born without functional lungs. Their first two children were born with that condition, so after that, they adopted.)<br /> So, basically, they are natural because &quot;God&quot; made them so. When the creation-diety (Gaia) makes you a certain way, you're as natural to that world as you can be.<br /> <br /> <u><b>A bunch of bullshit about how Dogs have a definite evolutioinary advantage over wolves , how tool use IS an evolutionary advantage, and a bunch of other garbage.</b></u><br /> Your friend didn't realize that Dogs are just Wolves who mankind bred for their own purposes?!<br /> Dogs are just tools created by man to do specific tasks they wanted.<br /> When it comes to &quot;evolution&quot; and &quot;tool use&quot;, the cosmology of the Universe comes down to &quot;there was balance, then the primal force of order wanted more power and twisted the force of entropy into becoming one of corruption instead, and that caused the universe to sheer itself into parts that were no longer balanced.&quot; Evolution and tool-use are formed because the Weaver has the power to move things along that course. Of COURSE tool use is an advantage. The Garou saw that and tried to wipe-out the Humans early on, but there were factions that argued against it and so the humans were allowed to make more tools, change the world, and become the greatest causes of the Weaver and the Wyrm's rise to power.<br /> While the Garou use tools and such as well, they've been slow (as a species) to adapt them into their cultures and ways (the Glass Walkers are obviously among the few who have adopted the idea of evolution, adaptation, and progress, and they're at odds with most of the Nation for that stance.)<br /> <br /> <u><b>oh some insanity about how environmentalism is the product of people who are not struggling to survive, and often considered gross hypocricy by those who are.</b></u><br /> This is a fun one to actually use in the games.<br /> Natural environmentalism exists, but not on a commercial level. Humans are, by their nature, greedy and survivors and will wipe an area clean of useful things and resources like a locust plague before they die off, or move on.<br /> Many &quot;environmental&quot; efforts actually use a LOT of resources to accomplish and can be just as devastating elsewhere--Electric Cars may mean less oil production and pollution from burning fossil fuels, but the mining for the materials, replacements of materials, and the energy to re-fuel those vehicles can be very devastating too. People aren't willing to work closer to home and bike/walk to work, people aren't willing to give up their luxuries en-masse, but they'll still buy a 48-pack of plastic bottles a week and put them into a recycling bin and feel like they're &quot;making a difference&quot; rather than just refilling a glass from the tap, even if it tastes funky. There is a LOT of hypocrisy in the mainstream environmental movements because people are greedy, short-sighted, and frankly just don't care... we'll burn the Earth before we consider that we're the cause and problems with it... all 9+ Billion of us.<br /> <br /> But how do the Garou fight against that? The Wyrm is everywhere, and it's even in the &quot;environmental&quot; movements in the WoD. Plastic companies that may claim that they are offering &quot;Earth Friendly&quot; materials may be poisoning the very plastic you're supposed to drink from on purpose, using slave-labor to produce them and creating more damage to the world in the guise of doing something that is &quot;good&quot;.<br /> <br /> To save the Earth, the Garou SHOULD follow the Red Talon's plan--kill the Humans... which would stop the Weaver and the Wyrm from having their greatest assets, but the Garou are so tied to a Human world that they just can't do it, and they'll fight against it... because whether or not they want to believe it, they're lost to their humanity.<br /> <br /> <u><b>ANOTHER peice of bullshit she had, was that lupus should be athiestic, since animals dont have religion</b>:</u><br /> Yep. Again, Garou just don't wake up as werewolves and go on to be &quot;natural&quot; werewolves running around and murdering things--not often at least. Also, I don't think your friend understood what a &quot;religion&quot; was either.<br /> Lupus are born as wolves. They aren't cognizant as Humans are, but they are ferally smart. THEN when they go through their First Change they are awakened to the world around them as the covers are thrown off of their eyes (similarly, when Homids are born, they don't have the animal instincts, but become aware of them when they go through their First Change.) Both are awakened to a new understanding of the Universe, but hued by the life they understood before their Change. No, Wolves don't have a religon, but they do have an understanding of the fundamentals of a feral world. When they are awoken to the world around them, they are brought into the life of being Garou, given a connection to the Spirits, to the primordial make-up of the Universe, and that their place was designed and destined by greater spirits.<br /> So, Garou aren't Animals, and Lupus aren't Animals either because they aren't Wolves, just as Homids aren't Humans once they go through their First Change either... they've become something greater.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Oh an argument that Garou are INFERIOR to humanity that I found really really sick.</b></u><br /> I can't really help with this one without more details... though in legends it was Humans who taught the Garou how to harness the elements in ways that didn't directly require the Spirits, but rather their understanding of natural sciences... you didn't have to ask spirits to create fire, but you could use friction, or flint/steel and make it happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T21:01:28-07:00","id":612994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Torakhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=612968#post612968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <u><b>A bunch of bullshit about how Dogs have a definite evolutioinary advantage over wolves , how tool use IS an evolutionary advantage, and a bunch of other garbage.</b></u><br /> Your friend didn't realize that Dogs are just Wolves who mankind bred for their own purposes?!<br /> Dogs are just tools created by man to do specific tasks they wanted.<br /> When it comes to &quot;evolution&quot; and &quot;tool use&quot;, the cosmology of the Universe comes down to &quot;there was balance, then the primal force of order wanted more power and twisted the force of entropy into becoming one of corruption instead, and that caused the universe to sheer itself into parts that were no longer balanced.&quot; Evolution and tool-use are formed because the Weaver has the power to move things along that course. Of COURSE tool use is an advantage. The Garou saw that and tried to wipe-out the Humans early on, but there were factions that argued against it and so the humans were allowed to make more tools, change the world, and become the greatest causes of the Weaver and the Wyrm's rise to power.<br /> While the Garou use tools and such as well, they've been slow (as a species) to adapt them into their cultures and ways (the Glass Walkers are obviously among the few who have adopted the idea of evolution, adaptation, and progress, and they're at odds with most of the Nation for that stance.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Caveat: some deleterious traits are dominant (or show other, more complicated patterns of inheritance). Familial hypercholesterolemia, for example. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Autosomal_dominant_disorders\" target=\"_blank\">There's a rather large list of them, actually.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T22:35:34-07:00","id":613039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Torakhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=612968#post612968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To save the Earth, the Garou SHOULD follow the Red Talon's plan--kill the Humans... which would stop the Weaver and the Wyrm from having their greatest assets, but the Garou are so tied to a Human world that they just can't do it, and they'll fight against it... because whether or not they want to believe it, they're lost to their humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is both wrong...and right. Yes, the Garou are tied to their humanity in that they've always needed humans to breed with in order to propagate their race, the same as they've always needed wolves.<br /> <br /> But it's wrong that killing off humanity would save Gaia (assuming that the Garou even had the capability to wipe out humanity at a stroke, which they don't) because such a wholesale slaughter of 7 billion+ humans would be such an astonishing atrocity that would feed the Wyrm like nothing else in history, the Holocaust included. The extermination of the human race would feed the Wyrm so much so fast that it would grow to such power that it would swallow Gaia in a single gulp (this is a metaphor for what would actually happen, but the point still stands). The Red Talons are 100% wrong when they say that killing off humanity would save Gaia. Remember, atrocities feed the Wyrm, and the extermination of the human race is <i>the greatest atrocity imaginable</i>. Sure, killing off all the humans on the world might stop the Weaver since it would be losing its favored children, but it won't stop the Wyrm. Yes, the Wyrm will be losing most of its minions hidden within humanity. But the atrocity of murdering an entire species of people will so feed the Wyrm that it will win by default. Remember, humans are Gaia's children too. Kill humanity and you effectively kill Gaia also.<br /> <br /> The Red Talons (as well as some other Garou in other tribes) simply can't or won't admit that the Garou's greatest collective mistake was the 3,000 year-long atrocity that was the Impergium. A major reason that humanity is so driven to pave over the world and tame its wild places is because the psychic wound of the Impergium and the resulting Delirium drove humanity collectively insane. Humanity fears the wild <i>because of the Garou</i>. As such, the Apocalypse is now imminent <i>because of the Garou</i>. The Garou are in danger of losing the Apocalypse War because their distant ancestors royally fucked up by starting the Impergium and some Garou to this day <i>still can't admit that</i>. The mistake wasn't ending the Impergium, it was starting it in the first place.<br /> <br /> So, no, killing off humanity won't save Gaia, not when it would make the Wyrm so powerful as to kill Gaia in a single stroke. The Red Talons are deluding themselves if they think that exterminating humanity will save them or Gaia. But then, the Red Talons are not especially stable, anyway.<br /> <br /> And while this might seem off-topic for the current thread, it's actually relevant because these mistakes made by their ancestors highlight the tragic hero nature of the Garou. &quot;<i>Your ancestors completely fucked up and that's why the world is in such a shitty state. Are you gonna repeat the mistakes of the past? Or are you gonna adapt and try something new?</i>&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":2710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","user":"Su-tehp","date":". 08-03-2015, 01:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T07:23:44-07:00","id":613343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me#post610887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I knew some ... jerk for a while who tried brainwashing me into thinking the garou arent heros.<br /> <br /> That environmentalism is garbage and some other bullshit.<br /> <br /> I submit myself for deprogramming</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Garou would not be heroes in the real world, and the kind of environmentalism they practice (violent destruction of many corporate entities and resources) would be bullshit in the real world, more likely to cause an angry reaction than a change in policy.<br /> <br /> However, in the world of darkness, with Pentex, and Gaia... then, if they beliefs are accurate, they are heroes, in that they are fighting at great risk to themselves, on the right side. But look up the Odessy and the classic tales; heroes don't need to be nice; they can be rapists and mass murderers, but still heroic and brave and on the good side. Of course, heroes can also be nice - that's allowed too ;-)<br /> <br /> Of course, if their beliefs are wrong, or partially wrong, that's another (interesting) story.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I should qualify by noting that in certain parts of the our world - certain indigenous people threatened by encroaching and violent corporations - the Garou tactics could be justifiable. Just not in general; most of these problems require political or economic solutions, not furry fighting machines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","user":"Cheesefondue","date":". 08-03-2015, 10:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","name":"Cheesefondue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T07:29:02-07:00","id":613346,"title":"","content":"To put it another way, Werewolf the Apocalypse is not a setting in which the horror movies are wrong and werewolves are the good guys. It's one where the horror movies are <i>right</i> and werewolves are still the good guys anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T07:32:33-07:00","id":613348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheesefondue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=613343#post613343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Garou would not be heroes in the real world, and the kind of environmentalism they practice (violent destruction of many corporate entities and resources) would be bullshit in the real world, more likely to cause an angry reaction than a change in policy.<br /> <br /> However, in the world of darkness, with Pentex, and Gaia... then, if they beliefs are accurate, they are heroes, in that they are fighting at great risk to themselves, on the right side. But look up the Odessy and the classic tales; heroes don't need to be nice; they can be rapists and mass murderers, but still heroic and brave and on the good side. Of course, heroes can also be nice - that's allowed too ;-)<br /> <br /> Of course, if their beliefs are wrong, or partially wrong, that's another (interesting) story.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I should qualify by noting that in certain parts of the our world - certain indigenous people threatened by encroaching and violent corporations - the Garou tactics could be justifiable. Just not in general; most of these problems require political or economic solutions, not furry fighting machines.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of their efforts don't exactly work out in the WoD, either. That's why the tag on the forum is &quot;how will you rage?&quot; rather than &quot;when will you rage?&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, what Garou practice is less environmentalism and more of a mythic struggle with surface trappings of environmentalism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T11:46:08-07:00","id":613740,"title":"","content":"About the &quot;environmentalism is a privilege of First World people&quot;... I see a certain amount of skirting the argument here. Personally, I see it exactly the other way round. In the First World, whatever inconvenience arises from environmental destruction, we can just throw money at the problem and life goes on. Climate changes, our crops don't grow properly one year, rainfalls flood a town? Let's just buy the tech to circumvent the consequences. Let's buy food from somewhere else, let's buy the medicine and vaccines against diseases that spread in devastated areas. Let's buy our fuels from other places in the world, no matter under which circumstances they're won and how many people get sick / cancer / have to be relocated during the production. Let's drive the climate change with all the energy that we waste and let the Third World, who barely contributed to it, bear the fallout while we get next to none. Watch islands slowly sink in the ocean and natural disasters kill hundreds of thousands. Let's just watch how hungry people destroy their environment, their forests, their soil just to survive. Environmentalism done right isn't just finger-pointing and being smug, it is essentially about tackling those problems by the root and realizing our own part in causing them in the first place. So I call major BS on that argument.<br /> <br /> Then, the Lupus should be atheists thing, it's even mentioned in the source book that what the Garou have isn't religion in the classic sense. It doesn't require belief, since Gaia and the spirits are absolutely real and tangible in that world. It's as if you could visit Jesus any time you want, have some coffee with him and talk about whatever. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Tool use: What's the argument here? Garou do that. Half human and stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/593/w20supporterhiddengarou.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3312,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3312-taci","user":"Taci","date":". 08-03-2015, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3312-taci","name":"Taci","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3312_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T11:47:08-07:00","id":613742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=613346#post613346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To put it another way, Werewolf the Apocalypse is not a setting in which the horror movies are wrong and werewolves are the good guys. It's one where the horror movies are <i>right</i> and werewolves are still the good guys anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's a setting where the horror movies got it right, but the moral ambiguity of the setting is so deep and pervasive that the very distinction of &quot;Good&quot; versus &quot;Evil&quot; is largely meaningless.<br /> <br /> If a Garou warrior (say, a Red Talon) goes out and slaughters a bus full of schoolchildren, simply because he<i> can</i>, does that make him (in the context of the World of Darkness) one of &quot;The Bad Guys&quot;? If you say yes, then what happens if the very next thing he does is sacrifice himself in a battle against a Wyrm creature that would otherwise have gone on to destroy or corrupt the area? If you say that the fact that he was willing to sacrifice himself for the spirit of the Earth makes him one of &quot;The Good Guys&quot;, does that then mean that him previously murdering a couple dozen schoolchildren is a moral act, or that it otherwise just goes away?<br /> <br /> The werewolves are monsters for the most part -- and the World of Darkness is a fairly complicated place.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T11:57:53-07:00","id":613752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taci</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=613740#post613740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then, the Lupus should be atheists thing, it's even mentioned in the source book that what the Garou have isn't religion in the classic sense. It doesn't require belief, since Gaia and the spirits are absolutely real and tangible in that world. It's as if you could visit Jesus any time you want, have some coffee with him and talk about whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>To sort of paraphrase Discworld, Werewolves believe in spirits the same way they believe in trees.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T12:50:27-07:00","id":613868,"title":"","content":"Some more bullshit she came up with is that humans are superior, because their able to CHOOSE their own destiny, not have one prescriped for them, that, running from is Generally considered quiting the game (As only a few chronicles WANT Ronin PC's)<br /> <br /> I showed her the game for a bit, over a decade ago back when VTT on AOL Was a big thing, at the start of 3rd edition... she played a bit but complained CONSTANTLY about basic things like the fact they were all fanatics, and how that to her eyes makes the setting dull.<br /> <br /> bullshit about animal attraction being rape.<br /> <br /> as it forces consent... far as I can tell it only does so as much as a seduction roll does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T13:14:46-07:00","id":613899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=613742#post613742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it's a setting where the horror movies got it right, but the moral ambiguity of the setting is so deep and pervasive that the very distinction of &quot;Good&quot; versus &quot;Evil&quot; is largely meaningless.<br /> <br /> If a Garou warrior (say, a Red Talon) goes out and slaughters a bus full of schoolchildren, simply because he<i> can</i>, does that make him (in the context of the World of Darkness) one of &quot;The Bad Guys&quot;? If you say yes, then what happens if the very next thing he does is sacrifice himself in a battle against a Wyrm creature that would otherwise have gone on to destroy or corrupt the area? If you say that the fact that he was willing to sacrifice himself for the spirit of the Earth makes him one of &quot;The Good Guys&quot;, does that then mean that him previously murdering a couple dozen schoolchildren is a moral act, or that it otherwise just goes away?<br /> <br /> The werewolves are monsters for the most part -- and the World of Darkness is a fairly complicated place.</div> </div> </div> </div>After killing a busload of innocent children who never harmed him or anyone else, then yes, that Red Talon is absolutely one of the Bad Guys. Because killing innocent people is bad <i>by definition</i>. The fact that the same Red Talon sacrifices himself against a minion of the Wyrm does NOT redeem him. History is replete with people doing the right thing for the wrong reasons and the wrong thing for the right reasons. Yeah, that Red Talon may have sacrificed himself and saved lives by killing that Wyrm minion, but that still doesn't bring those kids he murdered back to life. A noble monster is still a monster. Absolutely, that Red Talon is still a Bad Guy. After such an atrocity, one just cannot be redeemed. Some things just can't be forgiven. Once you cross the Moral Event Horizon (and killing a bunch of innocent kids is a textbook example of that), you're not coming back. Other Red Talons might not care, but plenty of the other tribes would throat that Red Talon on the spot for that sort of atrocity. A Child of Gaia, Black Fury, Bone Gnawer or Glass Walker sure as hell would.<br /> <br /> Of all the Tribes, while none of them are immune to falling to the Wyrm, it always seemed to me that the Red Talons are by far the most likely to fall. Genocidal urges and ideologies tend to have that kind of effect in the World of Darkness. Go figure. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=613868#post613868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some more bullshit she came up with is that humans are superior, because their able to CHOOSE their own destiny, not have one prescribed for them, that, running from is Generally considered quitting the game (As only a few chronicles WANT Ronin PC's)<br /> <br /> I showed her the game for a bit, over a decade ago back when VTT on AOL Was a big thing, at the start of 3rd edition... she played a bit but complained CONSTANTLY about basic things like the fact they were all fanatics, and how that to her eyes makes the setting dull.<br /> <br /> bullshit about animal attraction being rape.<br /> <br /> as it forces consent... far as I can tell it only does so as much as a seduction roll does.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand that the upcoming <i>Changing Ways</i> W20 book is going to talk about the religious fanatic mindset of the Garou. In a sense, the Garou <i>are </i>religious fanatics. Granted, their religion isn't conventional but they do place great faith in Gaia. And by any reasonable measure, they <i>are </i>terrorists in that they use asymetrical tactics in attacking sites staffed by civilians. Not every person working in a factory owned by Pentex is going to be a fomor. Some of them are just mundane humans working normal jobs who happen to get caught in the crossfire. And when they die, the Garou just shrug and say &quot;collateral damage&quot; and go back to their regular business, assuming that the Garou even break stride and notice the civilian casualties in the first place. The Garou might be fighting a war to save the world, but this is still pretty callous behavior that would be expected from any terrorist operating here in the real world. You can justify virtually anything if you think you're in a losing war with such high stakes.<br /> <br /> As for &quot;not choosing their destiny,&quot; it's true that Gaia chooses her Warriors, rather than them choosing Her. (There are more than a few Garou and Kinfolk who would dearly love to trade places, but can't. There's quite a bit of Kinfolk animosity from this alone.) Even with auspices, this is true to a certain extent: Luna chooses the roles that the Garou will have without consulting them before they're born.<br /> <br /> But then again, lots of humans don't get to choose their destiny. Some of them die from cancer before the age of 45. Some are killed in a car accident while they're still teenagers. Some overdose from drugs, others become teenage mothers, still others are murdered in an alley over $5. None of them chose their destinies either.<br /> <br /> More on this later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":2710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","user":"Su-tehp","date":". 08-03-2015, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T15:02:07-07:00","id":614090,"title":"","content":"I Didnt choose MS MS Chose me... I wish it would UNCHOOSE me.<br /> <br /> oh Yet ANOTHER Peice of BS, I know I started a separate thread on this, is why the government doesnt allready know everything about the camarilla and garou nation, and secretely pulling their strings, since neither is smart enough to be a celluour organization.<br /> <br /> My only answer is because &quot;Thats dull&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 08-03-2015, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T19:54:39-07:00","id":614466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=614090#post614090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I Didnt choose MS MS Chose me... I wish it would UNCHOOSE me.<br /> <br /> oh Yet ANOTHER Peice of BS, I know I started a separate thread on this, is why the government doesnt allready know everything about the camarilla and garou nation, and secretely pulling their strings, since neither is smart enough to be a celluour organization.<br /> <br /> My only answer is because &quot;Thats dull&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>MS? Multiple Sclerosis? I'm not sure what that has to do with your post, and I'm probably misunderstanding, but I'll let you explain it at your convenience.<br /> <br /> Anyway, to finish my post above, I'm not sure what your friend meant by humans being &quot;superior&quot; to Garou because &quot;humans can choose their destiny&quot; or whatever. To a certain extent, both humans and Garou can be helpless to change their &quot;fate.&quot; Hell, that's what the Dark Fate Flaw is for. And Garou, known for going into battle in a war from which they might never return, are essentially doomed from the moment of their First Change. And why? Because the First Change is essentially a draft into a never-ending war. once you Change, it's virtually guaranteed that you're going to die horribly and die somewhere likely far from home in a Hellhole or Wyrm-infested Pit where your remains will likely be violated by the Enemy. It's the very rare Garou who lives long enough to retire from the War (assuming that your tribe can afford or has the capacity to let you go and retire).<br /> <br /> But humans and Garou also have free will and the power to choose. Hell, the theme about making the right or wrong choices has always been a longstanding theme in Werewolf. So long as garou have free will, they have the ability to &quot;choose their destiny&quot; as well as anyone else. I'm not sure how humans would be &quot;superior&quot; to Garou in that regard, so I can't say I know what your friend was talking about, Prince.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T20:22:00-07:00","id":614484,"title":"","content":"The entire idea of coming here and presenting your acquaintance's statements so that we can tear them down or attack her seems odd to me. She doesn't like Werewolf, so what, she doesn't have to play. It doesn't sound like you've taken any of her arguments to heart anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T00:51:05-07:00","id":614701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=613899#post613899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Other Red Talons might not care, but plenty of the other tribes would throat that Red Talon on the spot for that sort of atrocity. A Child of Gaia, Black Fury, Bone Gnawer or Glass Walker sure as hell would.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the risk of starting another two-month argument with various other posters, and slightly off topic, I'm not sure I'd agree with that assessment (I <i>do</i> agree that the Talons' extra-curricular activities make them the villains, and no amount of self-justification or compensation can change that). While the Talons, Shadow Lords, and Get were the worst of the bunch, I've always looked upon the entirety of the Garou Nation (with the possible exception of the Stargazers) as being part of the problem too. In the above scenario, the Walkers probably wouldn't do anything unless the Talons did it in their immediate territory (and if they<i> did</i>, it would be to use Gifts and Rites to plant / create false evidence, or to intimidate witnesses into silence, and otherwise inhibit the authorities, rather than do anything against the Talons). The Gnawers probably wouldn't care unless it was a bus of poor, inner-city schoolkids, or BG Kinfolk. The Furies are also pretty apathetic when it comes to the Talons' mischief -- the two tribes are more often than not in lock-step about taking modern technological society down a notch. The Children are probably the biggest bunch of hypocrites. They preach the whole non-violence and peace-with-the-humans line, but they know <i>exactly</i> what the Talons are. Still, they are also dedicated to inter-tribal unity (including with the Talons), so when anything that the Talons do backfires, the Children are more than ready to give them healing and places to hide, rest and recuperate. Even when the Red Talons led the pogrom against the Bunyip and utterly exterminated them, the Children of Gaia kept on banging the unity-drum -- and then snapped up all the now-vacant caerns that they could get their paws on.<br /> <br /> Now, of course, the argument there is that the Garou need every tribe and every single last Garou warrior in the fight against the Wyrm, so they can't waste precious resources in &quot;pointless&quot; internecine fighting. It sort of highlights the complexity of the situation facing the Garou. But nonetheless, it brings to mind the old adage: All that Evil needs to flourish is for good men to do nothing.<br /> <br /> I have a hard time thinking of the Garou as heroic when half of them seem to think that murdering innocent people is perfectly okay, and the other half are too apathetic, contemptuous, indifferent, or just plain wrapped up in their own ideological B-S to do anything beyond the occasional mild verbal rebuke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T06:48:39-07:00","id":614968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=614484#post614484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The entire idea of coming here and presenting your acquaintance's statements so that we can tear them down or attack her seems odd to me. She doesn't like Werewolf, so what, she doesn't have to play. It doesn't sound like you've taken any of her arguments to heart anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes it should be, but a decade ago, back when VTT was a big thing on AOL She joined my game for a few months, and seemed to be thinking id be willing to adapt the game into something id have NO interest in running . like as mentioned before have Tame werewolves ued by the government, or have the CIA Secretly orchestrating things like Albrechts coronation etc.<br /> <br /> She said I was a Bad GM Not bending with my players. And that I essentialy, wanted others to act for me<br /> <br /> Sadly, that is what many Storytelling games amount to, as we go in with a specific story in mind, and a player whos a bad fit for it, is thrown out.<br /> <br /> she was so lazy, that she didnt even bother buying the book, and didnt bother learning terms like Rhya, Yuf, etc, she has some signs of creativity, why I didnt casually kick her out.... but kept making snide comments, trying to point out alleged facts, and got annoyed when I made a point of NOT incorporating them into the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T07:29:13-07:00","id":615045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=614968#post614968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes it should be, but a decade ago, back when VTT was a big thing on AOL She joined my game for a few months, and seemed to be thinking id be willing to adapt the game into something id have NO interest in running . like as mentioned before have Tame werewolves ued by the government, or have the CIA Secretly orchestrating things like Albrechts coronation etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Truly, that would be <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=C-CG5w4YwOI\" target=\"_blank\">a party in the CIA.</a>..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T08:20:59-07:00","id":615126,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Uniform Two Six;n614701]<br /> At the risk of starting another two-month argument with various other posters, and slightly off topic, I'm not sure I'd agree with that assessment (I <i>do</i> agree that the Talons' extra-curricular activities make them the villains, and no amount of self-justification or compensation can change that). While the Talons, Shadow Lords, and Get were the worst of the bunch, I've always looked upon the entirety of the Garou Nation (with the possible exception of the Stargazers) as being part of the problem too. In the above scenario, the Walkers probably wouldn't do anything unless the Talons did it in their immediate territory (and if they<i> did</i>, it would be to use Gifts and Rites to plant / create false evidence, or to intimidate witnesses into silence, and otherwise inhibit the authorities, rather than do anything against the Talons). The Gnawers probably wouldn't care unless it was a bus of poor, inner-city schoolkids, or BG Kinfolk. The Furies are also pretty apathetic when it comes to the Talons' mischief -- the two tribes are more often than not in lock-step about taking modern technological society down a notch. The Children are probably the biggest bunch of hypocrites. They preach the whole non-violence and peace-with-the-humans line, but they know <i>exactly</i> what the Talons are. Still, they are also dedicated to inter-tribal unity (including with the Talons), so when anything that the Talons do backfires, the Children are more than ready to give them healing and places to hide, rest and recuperate. Even when the Red Talons led the pogrom against the Bunyip and utterly exterminated them, the Children of Gaia kept on banging the unity-drum -- and then snapped up all the now-vacant caerns that they could get their paws on.<br /> /QUOTE]<br /> <br /> I think that a very macro view on a very specific situation. Sure the CoGs or what not as an entire tribe might not do anything about a pack of red talon killing a bus of children. But individual in a particular Sept might or possibly do. Sure Sept Alpha might condemn their actions.<br /> <br /> Every tribe has a party line but its interpretation is open to every individual in the tribe and the local Sept. Which is something that bothers me about many old OWoD gms who fail to take into account that the tribes in their majority are pretty open concepts and the individual is more than the tribe.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=614968#post614968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes it should be, but a decade ago, back when VTT was a big thing on AOL She joined my game for a few months, and seemed to be thinking id be willing to adapt the game into something id have NO interest in running . like as mentioned before have Tame werewolves ued by the government, or have the CIA Secretly orchestrating things like Albrechts coronation etc.<br /> <br /> She said I was a Bad GM Not bending with my players. And that I essentialy, wanted others to act for me<br /> <br /> Sadly, that is what many Storytelling games amount to, as we go in with a specific story in mind, and a player whos a bad fit for it, is thrown out.<br /> <br /> she was so lazy, that she didnt even bother buying the book, and didnt bother learning terms like Rhya, Yuf, etc, she has some signs of creativity, why I didnt casually kick her out.... but kept making snide comments, trying to point out alleged facts, and got annoyed when I made a point of NOT incorporating them into the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>So i am confuse, a woman who you meet on the internet a decade ago said a very ignorant view on the setting and 10 years later you want people to &quot;purge&quot; that view from your mind?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T08:59:03-07:00","id":615194,"title":"","content":"I may argue that the garou nation represents a failed attempt at holding the status quo, and that the proper heroes are the Black spirals, working to end the world and free all of creation of the crazed machinations of the weaver and a weakened gaia. <br /> <br /> That said, (yup I HAD to go there) the garou nation represents heroism on the saga scale. It's not and never about you, it's about something bigger then you. This even the spirals can recognize as deranged as they tend to be. <br /> <br /> A perfect example would be the short story &quot;a straw death&quot; (I think?) from rites of renown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T11:06:26-07:00","id":615320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=611102#post611102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">:A summary of her bullshit<br /> <br /> The garou are not sentient because their behaviour is controlled by a dice roller<br /> <br /> Their unnatural, because of their supernatural abilitys and the fact they cannot create healthy offspring with their own kind<br /> <br /> A bunch of bullshit about how Dogs have a definite evolutioinary advantage over wolves , how tool use IS an evolutionary advantage, and a bunch of other garbage.<br /> <br /> oh some insanity about how environmentalism is the product of people who are not struggling to survive, and often considered gross hypocricy by those who are.<br /> <br /> ANOTHER peice of bullshit she had, was that lupus should be athiestic, since animals dont have religion....<br /> <br /> Oh an argument that Garou are INFERIOR to humanity that I found really really sick.</div> </div> </div> </div>(I know this has already be quoted, and I usually don't re-quote when there's only a page or two and &quot;x&quot; has already been quoted, but this is so exceptionally bizarre that I felt compelled...)<br /> <br /> *What*?<br /> <br /> <i>What?</i><br /> <br /> <b>What?</b><br /> <br /> That is some very slanted, very ultra-biased bullshit somebody crammed down your RPG throat. And I am very sorry to read it. How utterly bizarre.<br /> <br /> &quot;<b>The garou are not sentient because their behaviour is controlled by a dice roller</b>&quot; -- Yeah, and? Of course they are sentient. The fact that dice are used to sometimes mimic the conflict between the various aspects of themselves (beast vs. man, et al) doesn't mean they aren't sentient -- it's just a game mechanic tool to help guide/simulate roleplaying. Or do your friends think that vampires (with their Humanity/Paths, and various Virtues) *also* aren't sentient, as they have a similar (if thematically different) &quot;dice-roller&quot; aspect? (Your friend(s) are nuts.)<br /> <br /> &quot;<b>The[y're] unnatural, because of their supernatural abilit[ies] and the fact they cannot create healthy offspring with their own kind</b>&quot; -- Unnatural? -- a matter of thematic perspective. In the Real World(tm), they would be unnatural, true, but that is neither here-nor-there in the WoD, where all sorts of critters exist. In *that* world, they are, in fact, &quot;natural&quot; in the context that the laws of Reality(tm) allow them to exist and do what they do, sans an &quot;proper&quot; breaking of scientific understanding (the &quot;science&quot; of WoD hasn't caught up with the Science(!) of WoD, which easily understands how Garou, and other Fera, exist). As far as reproduction, that is a human-bias if there ever was one: the whole point of their cross-reproduction is for the *uniting* of two aspects of life on Earth (Gaia/the Middle Umbra); that is, it *IS* natural for them to reproduce the way they do (alternating between human and lupine lineage/parentage), and unnatural for them to directly breed with each other (which is contextually the same as two full-siblings having offspring together... save that the spiritual aspect of the Garou ensures that such a coupling *will* result in &quot;something wrong&quot; with the Metis that results, whereas the incest of two siblings &quot;merely&quot; has a high chance of genetic defect). (Your friend(s) are nuts.)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">&quot;<b>A bunch of bullshit about how [d]ogs have a definite [evolutionary] advantage over wolves , how tool use IS an evolutionary advantage, and a bunch of other garbage</b>.&quot; Again, bizarre. Dogs have advantages over wolves primarily because of their domestication by man, *not* because of any inherent genetic superiority over wolves (save, again, for the domestication factor that is present in most dogs). Wolves are on the butt-end of things, currently, because of man, primarily, and not because of any other non-man-made factors. As far as tool use being an evolutionary advantage... well, *duh*, of course it is. But the thematics, as expressed in WW, tweak that concept a bit because the supernatural/paranormal is confirmable as &quot;real&quot; in that setting, and therefore the &quot;tool-use&quot; of the werewolves (fetishes, glaives, and the like) are mirror-valid to the tool-use of man, meta-conceptually. (Those two groups obviously disagree vehemently on various salient points, but the *concept* is valid for both.) (Your friend(s) are nuts.)<br /> <br /> &quot;<b>oh [and] some insanity about how environmentalism is the product of people who are not struggling to survive, and often considered gross [hypocrisy] by those who are</b>.&quot; -- This is bullshit on a level that is nauseating to the extreme. I am not even going to directly respond to it because YOUR FRIEND(S) ARE NUTS....</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">&quot;<b>ANOTHER [piece] of bullshit she had, was that lupus should be [atheistic], since animals don[']t have religion...</b>.&quot; -- *Animals* may not, but *Garou* (as a sentient species) certainly could/do. (Your friend(s) are nuts.)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">&quot;<b>Oh and [an]argument that Garou are INFERIOR to humanity that I found really really sick</b>&quot; -- Well, if I didn't have the above context of where your friend(s) were coming from, I 'd ask for an elaboration on this point because -- meta-conceptually -- there *is* a valid argument that can be put forth relative to that, if one delves deep into the metaphysics of the WoD and looks at things from a certain POV... however, given the further up contexts, I can safely assume that whatever would be said by her would be pure bullshit... leading me to the conclusion that <i>your friend(s) are nuts....</i><br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> The Garou, as a group, are as much anti-heroes as heroes, good guys as bad guys, know what they're doing vs. fucking up left-right-and-center, as most any other splat in the WoD. That is, many/most of them are trying to do what they *believe* is right and correct in order to save the world/Gaia... it's just that, like mortal man (and many other splats), they can be (and often are) wrong about salient details, have their own personal biases, and otherwise aren't as wise or understanding as they should be. That doesn't make them villains right off the bat -- it just makes them flawed relative to their goals/ideals. Not unlike most sentient beings in general.<br /> <br /> They can easily be heroes, and many are, from a narrative POV, and the game setting, as presented, assumes that relative to their individual and cultural understandings. Doesn't mean they don't/won't make mistakes, approach things from a mistaken perspective, or at times fall to the lure/rage of Dark Forces(tm) -- but by-and-large, they are the heroes (or at least protagonists) of their setting. Any other view ignores the narratives and themes presented in their (and other) books.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":1433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","user":"Just John, Forever...","date":".  spacing 08-04-2015, 02:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T11:26:09-07:00","id":615383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=614701#post614701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the risk of starting another two-month argument with various other posters, and slightly off topic, I'm not sure I'd agree with that assessment (I <i>do</i> agree that the Talons' extra-curricular activities make them the villains, and no amount of self-justification or compensation can change that). While the Talons, Shadow Lords, and Get were the worst of the bunch, I've always looked upon the entirety of the Garou Nation (with the possible exception of the Stargazers) as being part of the problem too. In the above scenario, the Walkers probably wouldn't do anything unless the Talons did it in their immediate territory (and if they<i> did</i>, it would be to use Gifts and Rites to plant / create false evidence, or to intimidate witnesses into silence, and otherwise inhibit the authorities, rather than do anything against the Talons). The Gnawers probably wouldn't care unless it was a bus of poor, inner-city schoolkids, or BG Kinfolk. The Furies are also pretty apathetic when it comes to the Talons' mischief -- the two tribes are more often than not in lock-step about taking modern technological society down a notch. The Children are probably the biggest bunch of hypocrites. They preach the whole non-violence and peace-with-the-humans line, but they know <i>exactly</i> what the Talons are. Still, they are also dedicated to inter-tribal unity (including with the Talons), so when anything that the Talons do backfires, the Children are more than ready to give them healing and places to hide, rest and recuperate. Even when the Red Talons led the pogrom against the Bunyip and utterly exterminated them, the Children of Gaia kept on banging the unity-drum -- and then snapped up all the now-vacant caerns that they could get their paws on.<br /> <br /> Now, of course, the argument there is that the Garou need every tribe and every single last Garou warrior in the fight against the Wyrm, so they can't waste precious resources in &quot;pointless&quot; internecine fighting. It sort of highlights the complexity of the situation facing the Garou. But nonetheless, it brings to mind the old adage: All that Evil needs to flourish is for good men to do nothing.<br /> <br /> I have a hard time thinking of the Garou as heroic when half of them seem to think that murdering innocent people is perfectly okay, and the other half are too apathetic, contemptuous, indifferent, or just plain wrapped up in their own ideological B-S to do anything beyond the occasional mild verbal rebuke.</div> </div> </div> </div>Entirely out of emotional reasons, simple pragmatism and the Litany would prevent any of those tribes being apathetic towards this.<br /> <br /> <i>Respect the Territory of Another-</i> Unless the bus was in Talon territory, which is most likely wasn't, the Talon would have had to do his deed in suburb or city area. In territory of another tribe's sept, who most likely don't approve of it.<br /> <br /> <i>Veil Shall not be Lifted- </i>Pretty simple, such a killing would risk the Veil.<br /> <br /> <i>Respect Those Beneath Ye, all are Gaia-</i> Even if some tribes argue against it, this is still the law. Needless killing of humans is not allowed, and any CoG, Gnawer or Walker philodox worth their salt would get the Talon for breaking this tenet.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T11:34:25-07:00","id":615388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=615194#post615194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may argue that the garou nation represents a failed attempt at holding the status quo, and that the proper heroes are the Black spirals, working to end the world and free all of creation of the crazed machinations of the weaver and a weakened gaia.<br /> <br /> That said, (yup I HAD to go there) the garou nation represents heroism on the saga scale. It's not and never about you, it's about something bigger then you. This even the spirals can recognize as deranged as they tend to be.<br /> <br /> A perfect example would be the short story &quot;a straw death&quot; (I think?) from rites of renown.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, &quot;A Straw Death&quot; from Rites of Renown II. I just finished reading it.<br /> <br /> What a waste. Selma charges into three packs of Spirals by herself when she knows reinforcements are on the way but doesn't bother to wait for them and gets herself killed? That's not heroism, that's stupidity. I could never see the &quot;honor&quot; in charging off into an unwinnable battle. All Selma had to do was wait a few more minutes and the Silent Strider would have returned with reinforcements and then Selma could have avenged her pack without dying, and thereby lived to gather more glory in more battles later on.<br /> <br /> This story could well have been titled &quot;Pickett's Charge: the Garou Version.&quot; Ok, I'm being sarcastic here, but when every Garou is needed, it makes no sense to throw your life away if it doesn't help you win the War. I never saw the point of a useless death. Gaia didn't give you the gift of shapeshifting so you could waste it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=615383#post615383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Entirely out of emotional reasons, simple pragmatism and the Litany would prevent any of those tribes being apathetic towards this.<br /> <br /> <i>Respect the Territory of Another-</i> Unless the bus was in Talon territory, which is most likely wasn't, the Talon would have had to do his deed in suburb or city area. In territory of another tribe's sept, who most likely don't approve of it.<br /> <br /> <i>Veil Shall not be Lifted- </i>Pretty simple, such a killing would risk the Veil.<br /> <br /> <i>Respect Those Beneath Ye, all are Gaia-</i> Even if some tribes argue against it, this is still the law. Needless killing of humans is not allowed, and any CoG, Gnawer or Walker philodox worth their salt would get the Talon for breaking this tenet.</div> </div> </div> </div>All good points. Yeah, that Red Talon would be in serious trouble for multiple violations of the Litany. Assuming he got caught, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":2710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","user":"Su-tehp","date":". 08-04-2015, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T12:15:29-07:00","id":615440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=615388#post615388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> All good points. Yeah, that Red Talon would be in serious trouble for multiple violations of the Litany. Assuming he got caught, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the amount of spirits that are doing watch duty in cities just for septs to -function-, they would get caught.<br /> <br /> But more, I find the whole 'Red Talon kills a bus full of kids' argument rather simplified. Red Talons -do- kill people, that is a fact. But they are still garou, they are not going to kill them 'just because'. And those who do? Usually fall to the Wyrm anyway. Most Talon human killing are humans who strayed close enough to territory, or Rite of Passages that don't always even work as some cubs end up liking the city and joining Walkers/Gnawers instead. And those tend to be the more extreme of Talon septs, most of them will just make the area unpleasant for humans.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T00:12:00-07:00","id":616040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=615440#post615440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Most Talon human killing are humans who strayed close enough to territory, or Rite of Passages that don't always even work as some cubs end up liking the city and joining Walkers/Gnawers instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoah. Red Talons defecting to the Bone Gnawers or Glass Walkers? I've <i>never </i>heard of this, but I'm curious to read it myself. Ana, do you have a page reference for this? (Considering the animosity between the Glass Walkers and Red Talons, I never thought this sort of thing was even possible. Hell, the idea itself just never occurred to me.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T02:41:10-07:00","id":616148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=613868#post613868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some more bullshit she came up with is that humans are superior, because their able to CHOOSE their own destiny, not have one prescriped for them, that, running from is Generally considered quiting the game (As only a few chronicles WANT Ronin PC's)<br /> <br /> I showed her the game for a bit, over a decade ago back when VTT on AOL Was a big thing, at the start of 3rd edition... she played a bit but complained CONSTANTLY about basic things like the fact they were all fanatics, and how that to her eyes makes the setting dull.<br /> <br /> bullshit about animal attraction being rape.<br /> <br /> as it forces consent... far as I can tell it only does so as much as a seduction roll does.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't help with the fanatic war. I DO agree here, Werewolf made it so ingrained it become kind of dull to me. But hey, it doesn't make them less heroic. And the part about destiny is very biased. On the setting the humans are making their own destiny, sure. The destiny of paving the way for the Wyrm to destroy the world. It is extremely out of context.<br /> <br /> By the way, it seems your friend plainly ignored all the context of the game. And sure, out of context the Garou are meaningless idiots, but so is anyone.<br /> <br /> The part on animal attraction is some more nonsense, though most players I know avoid this anyway. Something to do with the players being all humans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh Yet ANOTHER Peice of BS, I know I started a separate thread on this, is why the government doesnt allready know everything about the camarilla and garou nation, and secretely pulling their strings, since neither is smart enough to be a celluour organization.<br /> <br /> My only answer is because &quot;Thats dull&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that this is a game, that's actually the only true answer, and a valid one. But it DOES make some sense, as I said myself on the very other thread you put it. A government is just too big an institution to be as monolithic as some people think. The internal work to processes information is an unavoidable mess, too easy for such sensible information to be lost.<br /> <br /> Actually, probably a LOT of people in the government do now something about the supernatural side of the world. But they are scattered, without contact to one another, without access to one another's data, and each one with their own ideas abou what to do with what they know. Some fight the darkness. Some try to control it. Some are already puppets of the children of the night.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T03:15:34-07:00","id":616156,"title":"","content":"All said and done, well, I have a few things to add:<br /> <br /> 1- You and your friend just weren't on the same boat. Seriously, it isn't such a big deal by itself. She's better with a group that likes her ideas, and she will probably be a more productive player hem. And you are in the same manner better without her in the game, since she bothers you so much.<br /> <br /> 2- Her disagreement with the game runs deep. I think I found quite easily the source of the problem.<br /> <br /> She is Republican. Just that.<br /> <br /> Can't say I would agree with her on a political ground, but that's it, and there's nothing wrong with it.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't go as far as to say that WW makes political games, but the tropes on W:tA are fairly against republican ideals, and she seem's to like her game reflecting her political view.<br /> <br /> 3- Prince, I'm curious, tough, about what made you come here now, after ten years. We have a lot of things going on. You clearly tried hard to enjoy the game with her, is a lot frustrated, stressed because of the game and her ideas. Her arguments impacted you too much, even being total and clearly bullshit from the game POV. Here, by private message or at any other channel, you seem to have more to talk about this issue.<br /> <br /> Werewolf is a game. You and your friend are real people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T03:50:26-07:00","id":616197,"title":"","content":"Reading the OP, I don't even know why you took the words of your friends seriously...given that she probably does not seem to have an in-depth knowledge of the material. I simply do not get why you let a person like that even tell you anything about the Garou <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Double me being baffled by you taking her pseudo-fake-sciency talk as something applicable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T14:46:43-07:00","id":616811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=615440#post615440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But more, I find the whole 'Red Talon kills a bus full of kids' argument rather simplified. Red Talons -do- kill people, that is a fact. But they are still garou, they are not going to kill them 'just because'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering we're talking about a tribe that has a Rite whose sole purpose is reinforcing a Caern by torturing human victims to death over the course of several days, and the Talons are specifically written as many of them overtly using humans a prey (as in eating them), I respectfully disagree with your assertions. And in the interests of civility (since this disagreement sort of went down in a flame-fest last time), I shall speak no more on it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T14:52:30-07:00","id":616817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=616811#post616811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering we're talking about a tribe that has a Rite whose sole purpose is reinforcing a Caern by torturing human victims to death over the course of several days, and the Talons are specifically written as many of them overtly using humans a prey (as in eating them), I respectfully disagree with your assertions. And in the interests of civility (since this disagreement sort of went down in a flame-fest last time), I shall speak no more on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The rite in question is the province of one Camp, which isn't any form of majority among the tribe, and the Talons as a whole regard human meat as unclean..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T16:18:12-07:00","id":616872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=616811#post616811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering we're talking about a tribe that has a Rite whose sole purpose is reinforcing a Caern by torturing human victims to death over the course of several days, and the Talons are specifically written as many of them overtly using humans a prey (as in eating them), I respectfully disagree with your assertions. And in the interests of civility (since this disagreement sort of went down in a flame-fest last time), I shall speak no more on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Silent Striders have a rite that has brain eating to gain knowledge, but it is tied to a camp of Wyrm-tainted Striders. Similarly, the rite you are speaking of is tied to a camp of Talons who are VERY likely tainted. Then there are the maneaters, Bone Gnawers who eat human flesh. Every tribe has a nasty camp among them.<br /> <br /> As for eating, as Saur Ops said, Talons in general do not considers humans worth eating. Those who do have to clean it with a gift.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T20:28:10-07:00","id":617109,"title":"","content":"If were gonna talk tribal screw ups, let's mention the swords of heimdall too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T21:14:27-07:00","id":617126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taci</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=613740#post613740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the &quot;environmentalism is a privilege of First World people&quot;...</div> </div> </div> </div>To get a good idea of what some people are talking about when they say things like this, here is a <a href=\"http://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/05/opinion/in-zimbabwe-we-dont-cry-for-lions.html?action=click&amp;pgtype=Homepage&amp;module=opinion-c-col-left-region&amp;region=opinion-c-col-left-region&amp;WT.nav=opinion-c-col-left-region&amp;_r=0\" target=\"_blank\">good example</a> from an OpEd on the New York Times.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#333333\">In my village in Zimbabwe, surrounded by wildlife conservation areas, no lion has ever been beloved, or granted an affectionate nickname. They are objects of terror.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T05:34:00-07:00","id":617634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpa