d has bad art (holy FUCK, the reviewer really tears into the artwork! &quot;Porcuwolf, indeed...). And the author is less-well known than Shakespeare. And the CoG Revised book<i> is itself </i>a tragedy, while Shakespeare's tragedies were stories <i>about </i>tragic characters. And...<br /> <br /> And...<br /> <br /> And I think I ran out of comparisions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T12:51:39-07:00","id":617940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=617900#post617900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> According to <a href=\"http://projects.inklesspen.com/fatal-and-friends/kurieg/tribebook-children-of-gaia/\" target=\"_blank\">http://projects.inklesspen.com/fatal...ldren-of-gaia/</a> the CoG Revised Tribebook is on par with the Shakespearian tragedies. Except, the CoG Revised book is shorter. And less well-written. And has bad art (holy FUCK, the reviewer really tears into the artwork! &quot;Porcuwolf, indeed...). And the author is less-well known than Shakespeare. And the CoG Revised book<i> is itself </i>a tragedy, while Shakespeare's tragedies were stories <i>about </i>tragic characters. And...<br /> <br /> And...<br /> <br /> And I think I ran out of comparisions.</div> </div> </div> </div>It tells a lot that, after over 10 years between revised and W20, this is the thing that we speak of the most. Horrible as some camps might be, nothing beats horror created accidentally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T14:02:17-07:00","id":618056,"title":"","content":"I wonder if you can interpret CoG Revised as in-universe propaganda to discredit the tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T15:24:45-07:00","id":618148,"title":"","content":"The new supplement for the Award Winning game &quot;Lycanthrope: The Rapture&quot; from Black Dog Game Factory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T07:56:01-07:00","id":618870,"title":"","content":"I suppose a whole tribe does trump a camp as a mistake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T09:06:18-07:00","id":619009,"title":"","content":"I actually like the Red Talons, I have no problems with the tribe as a whole. Are there some that are freaking nuts yes. And yes I believe the blood letting rites are tainted, but make for excellent material for a story. Which is a lot more than I can say for almost the entire CoG tribe book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T09:27:34-07:00","id":619017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=619009#post619009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually like the Red Talons, I have no problems with the tribe as a whole. Are there some that are freaking nuts yes. And yes I believe the blood letting rites are tainted, but make for excellent material for a story. Which is a lot more than I can say for almost the entire CoG tribe book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeeah, thinking all Talons are human eating rage machines is like thinking all Black Furies kill men for rituals. It happens, sure, but its not -all- of the tribe. Red Talon's whole point is that they don't think breeding with humans was smart and are trying to remind the Nation that the ways of the wolf are important. Their current Rage is borne out of desperation due to their kin dying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T09:36:36-07:00","id":619022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=617634#post617634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let us never forget, Children of Gaia Revised Tribebook......an horrible tragedy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gaia have mercy...<br /> <br /> I had been able to keep that mentally locked-away for lo' these many years... and here it comes, a wash of perhaps-well-intended-but-<i>god-awfully-</i>written blargh that made me shake my head and feel *compelled* to read it because it was so bad it was like a massive car accident/pile-up -- you can't help but look at it.<br /> <br /> SMH...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T13:08:14-07:00","id":619302,"title":"","content":"I lied apparently. I will say one more thing on the Talons:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=619017#post619017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeeah, thinking all Talons are human eating rage machines is like thinking all Black Furies kill men for rituals. It happens, sure, but its not -all- of the tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, not <i>all</i> of them (the Whelps are an obvious exception), just <i>almost</i> all of them. Go back. Read the Talons again. It really is almost all of them.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=619017#post619017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Their current Rage is borne out of desperation due to their kin dying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which they themselves are almost entirely responsible for. They can make up any b******t justification they want, but the reality is that after the Impergium, they have only themselves to blame.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T13:54:20-07:00","id":619371,"title":"","content":"In a sense, both starting <i>and</i> ending the impergium were mistakes. Ideally it should never should have happened, but once it had been set up the later decision to set poor traumatised humanity loose on the world really did more harm than good.<br /> <br /> It's like generation 1 decided humans were a threat and turned them into dynamite, and then generation 2 realised that generation 1 were wrong, but tried to fix the mistake by burning it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 08-07-2015, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T17:04:00-07:00","id":619565,"title":"","content":"Given the time frame of the Impergium, it would technically be Generation 1 and Generation 1000 (or more; with a higher lupus population, you'd be seeing way more turnover on that front), but I concede that it doesn't really change the principle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=619302#post619302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I lied apparently. I will say one more thing on the Talons:<br /> <br /> No, not <i>all</i> of them (the Whelps are an obvious exception), just <i>almost</i> all of them. Go back. Read the Talons again. It really is almost all of them.<br /> <br /> Which they themselves are almost entirely responsible for. They can make up any b******t justification they want, but the reality is that after the Impergium, they have only themselves to blame.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, we know what humans did in this world, in real life, to actual wolves, and it's arguably worse, since the traumatized humans of the WoD apparent cluster even more tightly into cities (freeing up much more territory that would be covered in small towns in the real world) and the Garou have managed to secret away wolves in isolated pockets, such as the hidden mountain wilderness of Japan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T17:16:26-07:00","id":619572,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I didn't mean any specific generation. Probably should have called them A and B.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T17:46:47-07:00","id":619580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=619572#post619572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I didn't mean any specific generation. Probably should have called them A and B.</div> </div> </div> </div>3,000 years is about 100 generations (assuming 30 years or so is a generation. That's a rough human generation, yeah, not wolf generation, to be sure). So Generation 1 and Generation 100 would be accurate enough for our purposes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=619302#post619302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The [Red Talons] can make up any b******t justification they want, but the reality is that after the Impergium, they have only themselves to blame.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This. So much this. Whatever wolf-killing humanity did in the World of Darkness was (unconsciously/subconciously) in response to the Impergium. Humanity's desire to pave over nature is a direct result of humanity's desire to make the world safe. That instinctual desire comes from the Delirium. The Impergium created the Delirium, which drove humanity collectively insane. The Garou created the Impergium, which makes the Garou responsible the Delirium and everything that resulted from the Delirium, including humanity's pogrom against wolves. That's what makes the Red Talons into such tragic monsters. (Note here that I don't say &quot;tragic heroes.&quot; I find nothing heroic about the Talons because they're so genocidal.) Even after 12,000 years, they <i>still </i>can't see what they're doing wrong. And even if they could, they'd refuse to change because they've <i>always </i>refused to change. They know that adaptation is Gaia's oldest law, but, even as much as they love Gaia, they absolutely refuse to follow it out of some delusional belief that any change, adaptation or compromise on their part is a betrayal of Gaia. They are incapable of seeing that their stance is killing Her, and themselves right along with Her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":2710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","user":"Su-tehp","date":". 08-07-2015, 08:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T19:26:09-07:00","id":619658,"title":"","content":"The Talons however use the perhaps wrong view of the first extinction as the basis for the proof that the Imperium was correct. The Talons did not start it that would be the Silver Fangs. The Talons did not start the War of Rage that would be the Silver Fangs. The Talons followed the policies as loyal Garou. Most of the tribe still follow, but the dissatisfaction with the current status is growing. The other tribes treat them like carp, they spy on them, and anytime a school bus filled with kids is killed the first suspect will be any Red Talon in the area. Let's use the school bus example as a case.<br /> The massacre occurs in a rural area, a deserted highway that travels between Star City and Mountain Valley. The highway is near a Red Talon Sept. The highway has a horrible reputation, Bigfoot sightings lots of car wrecks, disappearing travelers, and other strange things. The Glass Walker Sept in Star City knows the Talons are responsible for a good number of these things. When the massacre happens on the school bus happens the Glass Walkers instantly blame the Red Talons. The CoG in Mountain Valley instantly back the Glass Walkers after all such a horrific thing had to be done by those savage Talons. The Red Talons while being pressured by both Septs to give up the guilty say fine it was Snarls at Shadows, a local Ahroun that is now dead having died at the local river where he fell to silver bullets stopping a truck full of toxic waste in being dumped. The Red Talons have no idea who actually committed the massacre but this lets them deal with the local Septs again. The Ahroun in question could have committed the massacre he and his pack where absent from the Caern that day. While the pack denys the charge, they are ignored. <br /> The Talons are easy scapegoats. So are BSD the entire incident could have easily been a Glass Walker cub that had his first change on the school bus or a CoG cub. Both tribes would have a vested interest in covering up the damage done by a first change Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T20:22:51-07:00","id":619709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=619658#post619658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Talons however use the perhaps wrong view of the first extinction as the basis for the proof that the Imperium was correct. The Talons did not start the Impergium; that would be the Silver Fangs. The Talons did not start the War of Rage; that would be the Silver Fangs. The Talons followed the policies as loyal Garou. Most of the tribe still follow [it], but the dissatisfaction with the current status is growing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you referring to the Red Talons still following the Impergium? But remember, the other tribes, including the Silver Fangs, abandoned the Impergium <i>9,000 years ago</i>. So the Red Talons are <i>not </i>being loyal to the Silver Fangs by continuing the Impergium. The Red Talons can't use the excuse of loyalty to the Fangs as the reason they still continue the Impergium. In fact, a Red Talon would be insulted by the notion that they still practice the Impergium because of loyalty to the Fangs. The Talons still continue the Impergium <i>because they hate all humans</i>.<br /> <br /> And what &quot;growing dissatisfation to the current status&quot; are you referring to?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=619658#post619658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other tribes treat them like crap,</div> </div> </div> </div>Please cite the evidence for this; I've never seen anything in canon that suggests the other tribes persecute the Red Talons. Yes, they're distrusted by the other tribes, but so are the Uktena, the Shadow Lords and the Glass Walkers. Hell, the <i>Bone Gnawers</i> are notorious among the tribes for being looked down on more than anyone else. You can't tell me that the Red Talons get more grief from the tribes than the Bone Gnawers.<br /> <br /> If you have proof of the other tribes treating the Red Talons &quot;like crap&quot; (which is a vague statement that is open to plenty of interpretation), please both cite a page reference from a published book and define exactly how they are being treated 'like crap.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=619658#post619658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[The other tribes] spy on [the Red Talons],</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, please cite evidence for this because I've never seen it. And the Red Talons are outright stated to have secret agendas that they deliberately keep secret from the other tribes. Remember the Winter Packs? Nowhere is it stated that the other Garou have even discovered the mission of the Winter Packs. That suggests that the rest of the Garou Nation isn't even keeping the Red Talons under any kind of surveillance. So where's your evidence that the other Garou are spying on the Red Talons?<br /> <br /> Please provide specific page references that the other tribes are spying on the Red Talons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=619658#post619658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and anytime a school bus filled with kids is killed the first suspect will be any Red Talon in the area.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, what? Who said this? Why would any non-Red Talon Garou in the area immediately suspect the Red Talons of killing a busload of kids when there could be any number of other suspects, including Wyrm minions? The bus school massacre was first mentioned as a hypothetical case, not an actual event that happened in canon, so it's not proof that the Red Talons are always going to be blamed whenever a bunch of humans get mass-murdered.<br /> <br /> Again, please cite any evidence you have that when a bunch of people are massacred, the Red Talons are the first to get the blame from the other Garou.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=619658#post619658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's use the school bus example as a [hypothetical] case.</div> </div> </div> </div>The bus school example <i>was first posted</i> as a hypothetical case by Uniform Two Six as to whether a Red Talon who murdered a busload of schoolkids could still be considered a hero if he sacrificed himself in a battle against the Wyrm after he murdered the schoolkids. (FWIW it's worth, I and a few others said no.) I think you meant that you want to use the bus school massacre in a <i>second </i>hypothetical. That's fine. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=619658#post619658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The massacre occurs in a rural area, a deserted highway that travels between Star City and Mountain Valley. The highway is near a Red Talon Sept. The highway has a horrible reputation, Bigfoot sightings lots of car wrecks, disappearing travelers, and other strange things. The Glass Walker Sept in Star City knows the Talons are responsible for a good number of these things. When the massacre happens on the school bus happens the Glass Walkers instantly blame the Red Talons. The CoG in Mountain Valley instantly back the Glass Walkers after all such a horrific thing had to be done by those savage Talons. The Red Talons, while being pressured by both Septs to give up the guilty [party], say &quot;fine, it was Snarls at Shadows,&quot; [who was] a local Ahroun that is now dead, having died at the local river where he fell to silver bullets stopping a truck full of toxic waste in being dumped. The Red Talons have no idea who actually committed the massacre but this lets them deal with the local Septs again.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the Red Talons deliberately lied to the other tribes and <i>threw a member of their own sept to the wolves</i> (pun intended) instead of just saying &quot;we don't know who did this?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=619658#post619658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ahroun in question could have committed the massacre [as] he and his pack were absent from the Caern that day. While the pack denies the charge, they are ignored.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ignored by whom? Ignored by the rest of the Red Talons, ignored by the CoG and Glass Walkers, or ignored by all three? And instead of blaming a dead member of the sept, why not just admit that they don't know who killed the bus school kids?<br /> <br /> And deception doesn't sound like a wolf/lupus thing to do. Red Talons know enough to keep their mouths shut about some things, but can they out-and-out lie? This is something I'd like to know, as I haven't read through the Red Talon tribebooks all the way through yet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=619658#post619658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Talons are easy scapegoats.</div> </div> </div> </div>But if the Glass Walkers know that the Talons are responsible for some of the murders on the highway, then the Talons aren't scapegoats, they're <i>probable suspects</i>. After all, the Talons have murdered people there before, so it's entirely reasonable to think that the school bus massacre was just another Red Talon attack. That's not scapegoating. Scapegoating is blaming someone who had nothing to do with what they're being blamed for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=619658#post619658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So are BSDs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering how depraved the Black Spiral Dancers are, it would be a very hard thing indeed to scapegoat the BSDs. Not impossible, but still. But what do the BSDs have to do with this hypothetical?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=619658#post619658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The entire incident could have easily been a Glass Walker cub that had his first change on the school bus or a CoG cub. Both tribes would have a vested interest in covering up the damage done by a first change Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>But covering up such thing is just another instance of maintaining the Veil. What would the CoG or the Glass Walkers get out of blaming the Red Talons for this? What would they have to gain by scapegoating the Talons here?<br /> <br /> It's not like the CoGs or the Glass Walkers are going to tell the humans that the Red Talons killed their kids; that would be a breach of the Veil. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Logically, the only people to whom the CoGs and GWs could say &quot;The Red Talons did this!&quot; would be the other Garou. What would the CoGs and the GWs have to gain by promoting intratribal conflict here?<br /> <br /> And this <i>is </i>an example of scapegoating the Talons, because here it was a First Change CoG or GW cub that killed the kids on the bus, but now you've created a <i>third </i>hypothetical where it was a CoG or GW First Change cub who killed the school bus kids instead of the Red Talons just being suspected of the bus school massacre but it's still unknown who actually did it. Let's just stick to your original hypothetical....<br /> <br /> ...wait, just what <i>was </i>the point of your hypothetical? You never stated a conclusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":2710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","user":"Su-tehp","date":". 08-08-2015, 12:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T21:06:01-07:00","id":619746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=619580#post619580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 3,000 years is about 100 generations (assuming 30 years or so is a generation. That's a rough human generation, yeah, not wolf generation, to be sure). So Generation 1 and Generation 100 would be accurate enough for our purposes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Impergium's start date got pushed back way the hell far in Revised, so it lasted way longer than a mere three millennia. Also, a human generation is about 20 years, so that alone would be 150, and that might only cover the Wars of Rage, not the huge chunk of time preceding them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This. So much this. Whatever wolf-killing humanity did in the World of Darkness was (unconsciously/subconciously) in response to the Impergium. Humanity's desire to pave over nature is a direct result of humanity's desire to make the world safe. That instinctual desire comes from the Delirium. The Impergium created the Delirium, which drove humanity collectively insane. The Garou created the Impergium, which makes the Garou responsible the Delirium and everything that resulted from the Delirium, including humanity's pogrom against wolves. That's what makes the Red Talons into such tragic monsters. (Note here that I don't say &quot;tragic heroes.&quot; I find nothing heroic about the Talons because they're so genocidal.) Even after 12,000 years, they <i>still </i>can't see what they're doing wrong. And even if they could, they'd refuse to change because they've <i>always </i>refused to change. They know that adaptation is Gaia's oldest law, but, even as much as they love Gaia, they absolutely refuse to follow it out of some delusional belief that any change, adaptation or compromise on their part is a betrayal of Gaia. They are incapable of seeing that their stance is killing Her, and themselves right along with Her. </div> </div> </div>Except that, again, we know how things turned out without an Impergium. It wasn't much better. If anything, the fear that made humans cluster closer together allowed the Red Talons to survive just a bit longer by making more territory into virgin wilderness where humans have never ventured. An explicit part of the atmosphere of the WoD is fewer small settlements and more people in the city, with more dark forests and foreboding stretches of plains and desert. What was actually wrong about the Impergium is that all the other Changers didn't put the Ratkin in charge of it, and that the Garou thought that they had done well by stopping the killing after committing genocide against the Fera that were meant to cull humans.<br /> <br /> Adaptation is a law of Gaia, but what kind of adaptation are we talking about here? It's hard to adapt to something if you die alone because you got crushed under a truck or shot, or if widespread toxins or poisonings kill everything around. The narrative of progress sounds nice and all, but if humans are going to spread far beyond their original ranges, kill fauna that would have controlled their numbers using tools, turn wetlands into cities with drainage problems while simultaneously trying to grow flat and level lawns in the desert... that's not something that adaptation can really help, especially when the lack of care exhibited by highway traffic for most living things cuts every habitat into tiny, marginal zones with the threat of death for ranging around. I guess that's an ironic twist benefitting the Mokole that don't need as much open territory, but it isn't a condition to which wide-ranging wolves can adapt. Even dogs would almost entirely be dead in no time if they had to run around without direct human support, and the Red Talons view domestication as an unthinkable crime, since it made wolves into a slobbery, obedient, puppy-like not-wolf. They get a massive uncanny valley effect just thinking about dogs, and they have for at least thirty millennia or so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 08-08-2015, 12:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T22:37:01-07:00","id":619802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=619746#post619746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Impergium's start date got pushed back way the hell far in Revised, so it lasted way longer than a mere three millennia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, no, it says in the Revised corebook, on page 28, &quot;The result was the Impergium, three thousand years of dominance over the human race.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, on page 54 of the same book, the Concord is defined in the lexicon as &quot;<b>Concord, The</b>: The agreement all the tribes reached nearly 9,000 years ago, after which the Impergium ended. The traditions thereof are still obeyed today.&quot;<br /> <br /> 9,000 years since the Concord + 3,000 years for the Impergium = 12,000 years. The dates of the Impergium and the Concord remain the same in Revised as they did in 2nd Edition. (We won't mention 1st Edition. That book said the Concord was <i>only 4,000 years ago, still within recorded history</i>, lol!....Wait, I just mentioned it after saying I wouldn't mention it. Crap.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=619746#post619746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that, again, we know how things turned out without an Impergium. It wasn't much better. If anything, the fear that made humans cluster closer together allowed the Red Talons to survive just a bit longer by making more territory into virgin wilderness where humans have never ventured. An explicit part of the atmosphere of the WoD is fewer small settlements and more people in the city, with more dark forests and foreboding stretches of plains and desert. What was actually wrong about the Impergium is that all the other Changers didn't put the Ratkin in charge of it, and that the Garou thought that they had done well by stopping the killing after committing genocide against the Fera that were meant to cull humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>My question is this: before the Impergium, were the Ratkin were already managing the humans' numbers by using disease and eating crops? Or is that something that the Ratkin began on their own after the Garou started the Impergium but before the War of Rage started? As I understand it, it was the Ratkin's original purpose to manage humanity's numbers through disease and loss of crops. Not to mention the added benefit of not having to resort to mass-murder to keep the humans' numbers down. So yes, you are entirely correct that the Garou screwed up by interfering with the Ratkin's job.<br /> <br /> Not sure about the other Fera being meant to cull humanity, though. As Gaia's &quot;immune system,&quot; the Garou are basically meant by gaia to destroy Her enemies (ideally, that wouldn't include humans since humans, as natural creatures, are Gaia's children too). But aside from the Ratkin, did any of the other Fera have a purpose involving humanity? The Corax and Camazotz are (and/or were) Her messengers, the Bastet are Her intelligence operatives, the Rokea cleanse the seas and endure, the Mokole are Her memory, the Gurahl and Grondr are her healers and cleansers, the Apis were her matchmakers for the rest of the Fera, the Ananasi belong to Queen Ananasa rather than Gaia, the Kitsune are a programming patch to help the rest of the Hengeyokai, the Nagah cull traitors to Gaia among the Fera rather than humans... Well, you have the Ajaba, who are reputed to have culled humans since they are called &quot;rainmakers&quot; because of the tears they caused to fall...but then the Ajaba were supposed to fulfill the Garou's purpose in Africa since most of Africa doesn't have wolves. But even counting the Ajaba (maybe) and the Ratkin as &quot;cullers of humanity,&quot; did any other Fera have the express purpose of culling humanity as such? Sure the other Fera cause the Delirium to an equal or lesser extent as the Garou, but I always interpreted that as the Fera having a similar &quot;primal imprint&quot; to the Garou upon a human seeing a non-Garou's Crinos form. In other words, the Impergium caused humanity to suffer the Delirium upon seeing <i>all </i>the Fera's war-forms, not just the Garou's war-forms.<br /> <br /> And if this is the case, then there's a more-than-likely possibility that the other Fera never participated in the Impergium at all. I seem to recall vague mentions that one or two Breeds, perhaps the Bastet, did participate in the Impergium, but then why would one of the Fera feel the need to follow a Garou policy, especially if the War of Rage had already started by this point? And I don't recall <i>any </i>mention of the Garou and any of the other Fera enacting the Impergium side-by-side, neither before nor after the War. Everything I've read in W:tA suggests to me that the Impergium was a Garou-only thing. And I don't count the Ratkin's eating of human crops as part of the Impergium because that doesn't involve mass murder nor any species-wide psychological damage that would be inflicted by being subjected to 3,000 years of exposure to such.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=619746#post619746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Adaptation is a law of Gaia, but what kind of adaptation are we talking about here? It's hard to adapt to something if you die alone because you got crushed under a truck or shot, or if widespread toxins or poisonings kill everything around. The narrative of progress sounds nice and all, but if humans are going to spread far beyond their original ranges, kill fauna that would have controlled their numbers using tools, turn wetlands into cities with drainage problems while simultaneously trying to grow flat and level lawns in the desert... that's not something that adaptation can really help, especially when the lack of care exhibited by highway traffic for most living things cuts every habitat into tiny, marginal zones with the threat of death for ranging around. I guess that's an ironic twist benefiting the Mokole that don't need as much open territory, but it isn't a condition to which wide-ranging wolves can adapt. Even dogs would almost entirely be dead in no time if they had to run around without direct human support, and the Red Talons view domestication as an unthinkable crime, since it made wolves into a slobbery, obedient, puppy-like not-wolf. They get a massive uncanny valley effect just thinking about dogs, and they have for at least thirty millennia or so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I guess I was pretty vague by what I meant by adaptation. I was thinking of a quote in the Red Talon 1st Ed tribebook. It was something along the line of a Red Talon saying &quot;Changing with the times to survive is Gaia's oldest law. It is the one law of Gaia we cannot obey.&quot; And I was thinking of the old adage &quot;adapt or die&quot; and the word &quot;adaptation&quot; was the only one-word-synonym I could think of to conflate the two. Perhaps not the best or most accurate choice on my part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":2710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","user":"Su-tehp","date":". 08-08-2015, 01:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T23:21:42-07:00","id":619812,"title":"","content":"Just for the record, the fact that humanity killed wolves IRL doesn't have anything to do with the setting, since the setting is fictional and establishes its own reasons.<br /> <br /> And the established fictional reason for that is the Impergium in W:tA. There are possibly other interpretations based on other game lines, but that wouldn't be valid from an Apocalypse POV.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T21:38:54-07:00","id":628199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Torakhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=612968#post612968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't sound like you need much re-programming because you realize that she was bat-shit-crazy, didn't have a real clue about the game, and apparently only read the game with the intent to argue against it like a conspiracy-nut (like the guy who has &quot;proof&quot; that Stephen King killed John Lennon through a government code placed in public magazines...)<br /> <br /> If her argument was simply &quot;Garou are not the heroes they think that they are in the World of Darkness&quot;, we could have a rational discussion regarding that standpoint, both from their way of seeing things, from the Fera, and from an outsider's view.<br /> <br /> However, she's arguing nonsense about the game mechanics, doesn't understand what a Lupus is, and so on.<br /> <br /> So, let's start with a few of the ideas you've brought up:<br /> <br /> <b><u>Garou are Heroic:</u></b><br /> In the World of Darkness, there are very few beings that are trying to save the world. Most are selfish, trying to fight for their own survival or advancement to live forever, or ascend. Only the Hunters (as a fat-splat) could be seen as being more heroic, putting their lives on the line to save the world from the monsters they perceive to be the world's demons.<br /> The Garou believe that they are the only faction that is actively fighting to keep the world from being destroyed by two of the primordial forces of the world (The Wyrm and the Weaver.) They were created to fight the Wyrm and are learning that they must also be aware of the Weaver's power and influence as well.<br /> They are TOO steeped in tradition and connection with their ancestors and spirits to change their ways very quickly. They are fueled by Rage and their own power at times and have done some really tragic and stupid stuff (killing off their Fera allies and making enemies of the survivors, Allowing 1 Tribe to be turned to the Wyrm, and being responsible for the destruction of the Bunyip because they didn't understand them and were tricked by the Wyrm into doing so.) They have been so blinded by the Wyrm that they ignored the rise of the Weaver as a nearly equal adversary. They also are so self-righteous and again so blinded by their traditions and mis-trust that they war among themselves over territory, meanings of their purposes, and the correct paths to take that they've also slaughtered their own kind to be &quot;right&quot;.<br /> Yet, for all of these issues, their unified purpose is to put their lives on the line to fight a war that will hold off the destruction of the world that has been foretold and guaranteed.<br /> <br /> <b><u>The garou are not sentient because their behaviour is controlled by a dice roller:</u></b><br /> Again, this doesn't make much sense, unless it was just how she meant to say that &quot;They are influenced by their Rage, and can Frenzy.&quot; Otherwise, it really doesn't seem like she understood character creation, or the mechanics of the game if she thought that a character's actions were determined by their rolls.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Their unnatural, because of their supernatural abilitys and the fact they cannot create healthy offspring with their own kind</u></b><br /> This sounds like an argument made by hunters (and not Hunters, who are imbued with supernatural powers to fight the rest of the WoD too.)<br /> In the setting and story of Werewolf: the Apocalypse, they are entirely &quot;natural&quot; because the primal forces of the world that decided what were &quot;natural&quot; created them to do what they do.<br /> The fact that they create Metis when breeding with one another is one of those &quot;rules&quot; that the forces that created them determined, and thus that's just part of their natural ways.<br /> We're not talking about designer-mutts here like Doodles, who can't be bred together or else they become genetically muddy. Think of it more as the True Born gene is recessive and when the True Born Garou gets the right genes and becomes True Born, their genetics require more diversity. There are plenty of real-life genetics where two people with recessive genes have a child that is deformed and that's perfectly &quot;natural&quot;, even though it's not optimal (a friend's parents both had a recessive gene that their children would have a 1-in-4 chance of being born without functional lungs. Their first two children were born with that condition, so after that, they adopted.)<br /> So, basically, they are natural because &quot;God&quot; made them so. When the creation-diety (Gaia) makes you a certain way, you're as natural to that world as you can be.<br /> <br /> <u><b>A bunch of bullshit about how Dogs have a definite evolutioinary advantage over wolves , how tool use IS an evolutionary advantage, and a bunch of other garbage.</b></u><br /> Your friend didn't realize that Dogs are just Wolves who mankind bred for their own purposes?!<br /> Dogs are just tools created by man to do specific tasks they wanted.<br /> When it comes to &quot;evolution&quot; and &quot;tool use&quot;, the cosmology of the Universe comes down to &quot;there was balance, then the primal force of order wanted more power and twisted the force of entropy into becoming one of corruption instead, and that caused the universe to sheer itself into parts that were no longer balanced.&quot; Evolution and tool-use are formed because the Weaver has the power to move things along that course. Of COURSE tool use is an advantage. The Garou saw that and tried to wipe-out the Humans early on, but there were factions that argued against it and so the humans were allowed to make more tools, change the world, and become the greatest causes of the Weaver and the Wyrm's rise to power.<br /> While the Garou use tools and such as well, they've been slow (as a species) to adapt them into their cultures and ways (the Glass Walkers are obviously among the few who have adopted the idea of evolution, adaptation, and progress, and they're at odds with most of the Nation for that stance.)<br /> <br /> <u><b>oh some insanity about how environmentalism is the product of people who are not struggling to survive, and often considered gross hypocricy by those who are.</b></u><br /> This is a fun one to actually use in the games.<br /> Natural environmentalism exists, but not on a commercial level. Humans are, by their nature, greedy and survivors and will wipe an area clean of useful things and resources like a locust plague before they die off, or move on.<br /> Many &quot;environmental&quot; efforts actually use a LOT of resources to accomplish and can be just as devastating elsewhere--Electric Cars may mean less oil production and pollution from burning fossil fuels, but the mining for the materials, replacements of materials, and the energy to re-fuel those vehicles can be very devastating too. People aren't willing to work closer to home and bike/walk to work, people aren't willing to give up their luxuries en-masse, but they'll still buy a 48-pack of plastic bottles a week and put them into a recycling bin and feel like they're &quot;making a difference&quot; rather than just refilling a glass from the tap, even if it tastes funky. There is a LOT of hypocrisy in the mainstream environmental movements because people are greedy, short-sighted, and frankly just don't care... we'll burn the Earth before we consider that we're the cause and problems with it... all 9+ Billion of us.<br /> <br /> But how do the Garou fight against that? The Wyrm is everywhere, and it's even in the &quot;environmental&quot; movements in the WoD. Plastic companies that may claim that they are offering &quot;Earth Friendly&quot; materials may be poisoning the very plastic you're supposed to drink from on purpose, using slave-labor to produce them and creating more damage to the world in the guise of doing something that is &quot;good&quot;.<br /> <br /> To save the Earth, the Garou SHOULD follow the Red Talon's plan--kill the Humans... which would stop the Weaver and the Wyrm from having their greatest assets, but the Garou are so tied to a Human world that they just can't do it, and they'll fight against it... because whether or not they want to believe it, they're lost to their humanity.<br /> <br /> <u><b>ANOTHER peice of bullshit she had, was that lupus should be athiestic, since animals dont have religion</b>:</u><br /> Yep. Again, Garou just don't wake up as werewolves and go on to be &quot;natural&quot; werewolves running around and murdering things--not often at least. Also, I don't think your friend understood what a &quot;religion&quot; was either.<br /> Lupus are born as wolves. They aren't cognizant as Humans are, but they are ferally smart. THEN when they go through their First Change they are awakened to the world around them as the covers are thrown off of their eyes (similarly, when Homids are born, they don't have the animal instincts, but become aware of them when they go through their First Change.) Both are awakened to a new understanding of the Universe, but hued by the life they understood before their Change. No, Wolves don't have a religon, but they do have an understanding of the fundamentals of a feral world. When they are awoken to the world around them, they are brought into the life of being Garou, given a connection to the Spirits, to the primordial make-up of the Universe, and that their place was designed and destined by greater spirits.<br /> So, Garou aren't Animals, and Lupus aren't Animals either because they aren't Wolves, just as Homids aren't Humans once they go through their First Change either... they've become something greater.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Oh an argument that Garou are INFERIOR to humanity that I found really really sick.</b></u><br /> I can't really help with this one without more details... though in legends it was Humans who taught the Garou how to harness the elements in ways that didn't directly require the Spirits, but rather their understanding of natural sciences... you didn't have to ask spirits to create fire, but you could use friction, or flint/steel and make it happen.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry to bump this thread after over a week, been hospitalized, sadly, MS is not going to unchose me, as much as I'd like it to.<br /> <br /> She attacked the idea garou are greater then humanity whenever I reffered to it casually, as a given she attacked the notion, ruthlessly.<br /> <br /> She also got feisty about silver, saying you should be able to make them melt with photo ink, and demanding to know the quantity and purity of silver, to injure them.<br /> <br /> I had been trying to explain the game to her, at first she was ok, then she got increasingly critical and scathing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T21:43:31-07:00","id":628201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=615320#post615320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I know this has already be quoted, and I usually don't re-quote when there's only a page or two and &quot;x&quot; has already been quoted, but this is so exceptionally bizarre that I felt compelled...)<br /> <br /> *What*?<br /> <br /> <i>What?</i><br /> <br /> <b>What?</b><br /> <br /> That is some very slanted, very ultra-biased bullshit somebody crammed down your RPG throat. And I am very sorry to read it. How utterly bizarre.<br /> <br /> &quot;<b>The garou are not sentient because their behaviour is controlled by a dice roller</b>&quot; -- Yeah, and? Of course they are sentient. The fact that dice are used to sometimes mimic the conflict between the various aspects of themselves (beast vs. man, et al) doesn't mean they aren't sentient -- it's just a game mechanic tool to help guide/simulate roleplaying. Or do your friends think that vampires (with their Humanity/Paths, and various Virtues) *also* aren't sentient, as they have a similar (if thematically different) &quot;dice-roller&quot; aspect? (Your friend(s) are nuts.)<br /> <br /> &quot;<b>The[y're] unnatural, because of their supernatural abilit[ies] and the fact they cannot create healthy offspring with their own kind</b>&quot; -- Unnatural? -- a matter of thematic perspective. In the Real World(tm), they would be unnatural, true, but that is neither here-nor-there in the WoD, where all sorts of critters exist. In *that* world, they are, in fact, &quot;natural&quot; in the context that the laws of Reality(tm) allow them to exist and do what they do, sans an &quot;proper&quot; breaking of scientific understanding (the &quot;science&quot; of WoD hasn't caught up with the Science(!) of WoD, which easily understands how Garou, and other Fera, exist). As far as reproduction, that is a human-bias if there ever was one: the whole point of their cross-reproduction is for the *uniting* of two aspects of life on Earth (Gaia/the Middle Umbra); that is, it *IS* natural for them to reproduce the way they do (alternating between human and lupine lineage/parentage), and unnatural for them to directly breed with each other (which is contextually the same as two full-siblings having offspring together... save that the spiritual aspect of the Garou ensures that such a coupling *will* result in &quot;something wrong&quot; with the Metis that results, whereas the incest of two siblings &quot;merely&quot; has a high chance of genetic defect). (Your friend(s) are nuts.)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">&quot;<b>A bunch of bullshit about how [d]ogs have a definite [evolutionary] advantage over wolves , how tool use IS an evolutionary advantage, and a bunch of other garbage</b>.&quot; Again, bizarre. Dogs have advantages over wolves primarily because of their domestication by man, *not* because of any inherent genetic superiority over wolves (save, again, for the domestication factor that is present in most dogs). Wolves are on the butt-end of things, currently, because of man, primarily, and not because of any other non-man-made factors. As far as tool use being an evolutionary advantage... well, *duh*, of course it is. But the thematics, as expressed in WW, tweak that concept a bit because the supernatural/paranormal is confirmable as &quot;real&quot; in that setting, and therefore the &quot;tool-use&quot; of the werewolves (fetishes, glaives, and the like) are mirror-valid to the tool-use of man, meta-conceptually. (Those two groups obviously disagree vehemently on various salient points, but the *concept* is valid for both.) (Your friend(s) are nuts.)<br /> <br /> &quot;<b>oh [and] some insanity about how environmentalism is the product of people who are not struggling to survive, and often considered gross [hypocrisy] by those who are</b>.&quot; -- This is bullshit on a level that is nauseating to the extreme. I am not even going to directly respond to it because YOUR FRIEND(S) ARE NUTS....</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">&quot;<b>ANOTHER [piece] of bullshit she had, was that lupus should be [atheistic], since animals don[']t have religion...</b>.&quot; -- *Animals* may not, but *Garou* (as a sentient species) certainly could/do. (Your friend(s) are nuts.)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">&quot;<b>Oh and [an]argument that Garou are INFERIOR to humanity that I found really really sick</b>&quot; -- Well, if I didn't have the above context of where your friend(s) were coming from, I 'd ask for an elaboration on this point because -- meta-conceptually -- there *is* a valid argument that can be put forth relative to that, if one delves deep into the metaphysics of the WoD and looks at things from a certain POV... however, given the further up contexts, I can safely assume that whatever would be said by her would be pure bullshit... leading me to the conclusion that <i>your friend(s) are nuts....</i><br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> The Garou, as a group, are as much anti-heroes as heroes, good guys as bad guys, know what they're doing vs. fucking up left-right-and-center, as most any other splat in the WoD. That is, many/most of them are trying to do what they *believe* is right and correct in order to save the world/Gaia... it's just that, like mortal man (and many other splats), they can be (and often are) wrong about salient details, have their own personal biases, and otherwise aren't as wise or understanding as they should be. That doesn't make them villains right off the bat -- it just makes them flawed relative to their goals/ideals. Not unlike most sentient beings in general.<br /> <br /> They can easily be heroes, and many are, from a narrative POV, and the game setting, as presented, assumes that relative to their individual and cultural understandings. Doesn't mean they don't/won't make mistakes, approach things from a mistaken perspective, or at times fall to the lure/rage of Dark Forces(tm) -- but by-and-large, they are the heroes (or at least protagonists) of their setting. Any other view ignores the narratives and themes presented in their (and other) books.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yes she DOES think Kindred are not sentient, or changelings or ANYONE whos behaviour can be simulated with a dice roller<br /> <br /> she takes it as a given... and has this maddening habbit of making sense, <br /> <br /> She dissapeared a few months ago... I blocked her on aol. If I dont check to see if shes on I'll forget she exists hopefully<br /> <br /> As I cant seek her counsel anymore<br /> <br /> I HATE HER so much<br /> <br /> she ruined things so contempuously<br /> <br /> why Did I not do this earlier?<br /> <br /> because shes like the golden asp in exalted.<br /> <br /> Her advise is often prudent, and those who follow it will prosper... but will fall prey to bitter cynicism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T12:35:46-07:00","id":634946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=628201#post628201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Yes she DOES think Kindred are not sentient, or changelings or ANYONE whos behaviour can be simulated with a dice roller<br /> <br /> she takes it as a given... and has this maddening habbit of making sense,<br /> <br /> She dissapeared a few months ago... I blocked her on aol. If I dont check to see if shes on I'll forget she exists hopefully<br /> <br /> As I cant seek her counsel anymore<br /> <br /> I HATE HER so much<br /> <br /> she ruined things so contempuously<br /> <br /> why Did I not do this earlier?<br /> <br /> because shes like the golden asp in exalted.<br /> <br /> Her advise is often prudent, and those who follow it will prosper... but will fall prey to bitter cynicism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okaaaayyyy....<br /> <br /> Now, *you* are starting to sound a little out there. But in any case, hope you have her &quot;programming&quot; out of your head... otherwise, she's just proving that *you* &quot;aren't sentient&quot;, as she can &quot;dice-roll&quot; you into believing x, y and z without there being any proper volition or cognizance on your part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T14:29:47-07:00","id":635071,"title":"","content":"I don't know where this &quot;maddening habit of making sense&quot; is supposed to be because from what you've told us she just spouts a stream of easily-disproven bullshit.<br /> <br /> Seriously, it's like she doesn't even grasp the concept of gaming abstractions. I mean, how else are you supposed to model anger management issues?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T14:36:05-07:00","id":635075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=628201#post628201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-ic