avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T19:45:27-07:00","id":636568,"title":"","content":"That's how the guy reaches for help, let him be.<br /> <br /> <b>Prince of the Night</b>, what else she did or said that annoyed you so much?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T21:42:49-07:00","id":636673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=628199#post628199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sorry to bump this thread after over a week, been hospitalized, sadly, MS is not going to unchose me, as much as I'd like it to.<br /> <br /> She attacked the idea garou are greater then humanity whenever I reffered to it casually, as a given she attacked the notion, ruthlessly.<br /> <br /> She also got feisty about silver, saying you should be able to make them melt with photo ink, and demanding to know the quantity and purity of silver, to injure them.<br /> <br /> I had been trying to explain the game to her, at first she was ok, then she got increasingly critical and scathing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry to hear about your medical troubles. Hope things improve for you.<br /> <br /> Now, she may well have been very condescending about it, but one has to concede that saying Garou are &quot;greater than&quot; humanity is a rather broad and subjective statement. At least in the absence of more specifics.<br /> <br /> The question of how much and how pure silver must be is a debate I've seen in multiple games for over a decade. Its a legitimate question, though again I can imagine her attitude about it may not have been the most genteel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T21:46:36-07:00","id":636676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=636673#post636673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question of how much and how pure silver must be is a debate I've seen in multiple games for over a decade. Its a legitimate question, though again I can imagine her attitude about it may not have been the most genteel.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, W20 settled what Revised left still somewhat open. It has to be around 90% pure, minimum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T21:56:06-07:00","id":636680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=636676#post636676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the other hand, W20 settled what Revised left still somewhat open. It has to be around 90% pure, minimum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good start! I've yet to play in any W20 games myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T11:39:18-07:00","id":637190,"title":"","content":"I think that talking about silver purity in terms of percentages is too scientific. They question is whether the substance is spiritually silver, which should be answered in terms of rather a reasonable layperson would consider a substance to be silver. A silver based compound (like silver halide film, silver nitrate, colloidal silver, etc.) should never count as true silver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T11:46:46-07:00","id":637193,"title":"","content":"How about &quot;90% will generally do it, but you'll get away with less if the object really resonates with silver on a spiritual level.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T12:05:03-07:00","id":637223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=637190#post637190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that talking about silver purity in terms of percentages is too scientific. They question is whether the substance is spiritually silver, which should be answered in terms of rather a reasonable layperson would consider a substance to be silver. A silver based compound (like silver halide film, silver nitrate, colloidal silver, etc.) should never count as true silver.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a better starting point than &quot;I don't really know how much.&quot; None of those compounds would likely be admitted anyway, since the reference point in the book was to sterling silver, which is 92.5% silver by mass, determined most often by measuring weight. Silver halide, even if you were trying to squirm around the spiritual nature of things, is far less than 92.5% silver by weight, as are silver halides and most every form of silver colloidal compound. At that point, adding on &quot;no compounds, ions, or the like&quot; is just icing on the cake.<br /> <br /> Size of the object probably also figures into it, but that's an ill-explored level of detail. I'd imagine that it'd be really important for Mokole, since they can get really, really huge, and having a single, comparatively tiny silver or gold bullet ruin your kaijuu rampage would be startlingly anticlimactic for any game. A shell would be more reasonable, but it wouldn't be dealing out that damage to a 98-meter tall monster that it does to a merely 7.6-meter long tank.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T21:49:03-07:00","id":639839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=615388#post615388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, &quot;A Straw Death&quot; from Rites of Renown II. I just finished reading it.<br /> <br /> What a waste. Selma charges into three packs of Spirals by herself when she knows reinforcements are on the way but doesn't bother to wait for them and gets herself killed? That's not heroism, that's stupidity. I could never see the &quot;honor&quot; in charging off into an unwinnable battle. All Selma had to do was wait a few more minutes and the Silent Strider would have returned with reinforcements and then Selma could have avenged her pack without dying, and thereby lived to gather more glory in more battles later on.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>The story has a lot of cultural baggage. I saw the whole point of the story as being a chance to illustrate Fenrir culture, what's often described as their &quot;fatalism.&quot; It's a culture that, like their Viking ancestors, places a higher value on dying in battle than dying in your bed of old age. She debates the strategy of the situation with herself, but in the end, she chooses Fenrir valor over strategy and even family. It was a perfect way to illustrate the often-repeated clich\u00e9 that a Fenrir &quot;would gladly allow themselves to be devoured by a Wyrm demon just so they could rip out its tongue before they died.&quot; Most warrior cultures have some version of the idea that strategy and circumstance are sometimes subservient to the sole focus of a warrior: the destruction of your opponent.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying it was the wisest choice, it's just the most Fenrir thing to do. It reminded me of the end of &quot;The 13th Warrior.&quot; Or maybe &quot;300,&quot; a perfect example of how charging off into an unwinnable battle can have a greater purpose.<br /> <br /> And whether or not she died is never confirmed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7445-viking-funeral","name":"Viking Funeral","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7445_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T00:19:27-07:00","id":641249,"title":"","content":"In 300 the unwinnable battle was actually a strategic decision, so I don't think it marries well there. The Spartans are willing to die in glory, but not to sacrifice strategy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T00:23:10-07:00","id":641252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=641249#post641249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 300 the unwinnable battle was actually a strategic decision, so I don't think it marries well there. The Spartans are willing to die in glory, but not to sacrifice strategy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hilarious, considering that their core ethos proved to be a strategic blunder of the highest order when they got grabby and wanted to control more territory. You can't really do that if you only have a small number of troops, no matter how &quot;elite&quot; they might be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T08:23:29-07:00","id":641600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=641252#post641252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hilarious, considering that their core ethos proved to be a strategic blunder of the highest order when they got grabby and wanted to control more territory. You can't really do that if you only have a small number of troops, no matter how &quot;elite&quot; they might be.</div> </div> </div> </div>(Just jumping back in b/c I forgot about #Bailing on this thread... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> That had more to do with arrogance/hubris, in that context -- they thought that a few hundred/thousand of *their* troops would outclass multiples-more of other groups... which, of course, eventually backfired on them. They still had strategy/strategic values, it's just that much like, in game terms, with the Order of Hermes, they let their hubris get in the way over time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T15:37:01-07:00","id":643470,"title":"","content":"History is full of situations where people should know better. Rome and emperor Valens shouldn't have fallen to the goths, but they were routed terribly, and all to arrogance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T11:51:21-07:00","id":644458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=641252#post641252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hilarious, considering that their core ethos proved to be a strategic blunder of the highest order when they got grabby and wanted to control more territory. You can't really do that if you only have a small number of troops, no matter how &quot;elite&quot; they might be.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=641600#post641600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Just jumping back in b/c I forgot about #Bailing on this thread... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> That had more to do with arrogance/hubris, in that context -- they thought that a few hundred/thousand of *their* troops would outclass multiples-more of other groups... which, of course, eventually backfired on them. They still had strategy/strategic values, it's just that much like, in game terms, with the Order of Hermes, they let their hubris get in the way over time.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a bit off-topic, but I feel I have to mention something related to this. I don't know if any of you guys are fans of The Order of the Stick webcomic, but if any of you have read the Start of Darkness OOTS prequel book, you'll recognize the idea that Xykon espouses his whole martial philosophy (such as it is).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hey, you know what really gets under my skin? <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/IWouldSayIfICouldSay\" target=\"_blank\">Proverbially, of course?</a> <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ScrewYouElves\" target=\"_blank\">A century of wizards looking down their damn noses at me</a>. Energy Drain! I know people think I'm stupid. Because I'm not a wizard. <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ObfuscatingStupidity\" target=\"_blank\">Because I get bored easily.</a> <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/BrilliantButLazy\" target=\"_blank\">Because I have no interest in strategy or tactics or contingency planning</a>. Energy Drain! But see, I've learned a lot over the years since I died. A lot more than I learned during my life. And now I see that planning doesn't matter. Strategy doesn't matter. Only two things matter: Force in as great a concentration as you can manage, and style. And in a pinch, style can slide. Energy Drain! In any battle, there's always a level of force against which no tactics can succeed. For example, all I need to do is keep smacking you with Energy Drains, and soon you won't be able to cast any of your fancy spells at all. Energy Drain! <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/UnequalRites\" target=\"_blank\">Because yes, I am a sorcerer - and this magic is in my bones, not cribbed off of &quot;Magic for Dummies.&quot;</a> <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/NoHoldsBarredBeatdown\" target=\"_blank\">And I can keep casting the same friggin' spell at you until you roll over and die.</a> <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/IronicEcho\" target=\"_blank\">You can have your finely-crafted watch -</a> <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/WhenAllYouHaveIsAHammer\" target=\"_blank\">give me the sledgehammer to the face any day</a>. ENERGY DRAIN! </div> </div> </div>Yeah, no matter how elite or badass your troops may be, if there just aren't enough of them, there will eventually be a level of force large enough that they just won't be able to overcome. Quantity begets a quality all its own. Bigger sometimes really is better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T05:27:40-07:00","id":646562,"title":"","content":"I'm quite surprised reading this thread.<br /> <br /> With all my respect, I think you are being close minded, and you want to remain so. Your friend is either trolling you or playing the devils advocate to offer you new perspective. Your reaction is anger because she threw some doubt and submiting yourself to reprogramming.<br /> <br /> What is even worse, I have read someone that instead of advicing you to cool down and accept other perspectives, they encourage you to avoid this person and never talk to her again. That is really crazy, I'm sorry to say. First, this is just a game, the Garou aren't heroes, nor they are nothing because they don't exist. It would be disastrous if you broke relationships with someone just because of her opinion about somehting fictional. Second, even if you were discussing something real, even if you were discussing something important, you have to learn to deal with different opinions without enraging yourself or asking people to reasure your previous beliefs.<br /> <br /> But, let me please continue playing devil's advocate because I find the Garou to be one of the greatest villains in the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> <b>The garou are not sentient because their behaviour is controlled by a dice roller</b><br /> <br /> As every have told, that not make sense. But let me use some of the idea. Reading the WtA material, I find that they can be sentient, but they have a lack of free will. We are told that every Werewolf knows inside that all the Gaia/Triat story is true. It is firmly programmed into them, so they don't have freedom to think their own interpretation of the world. We don't even know if that &quot;truth&quot; hardwired in their brains is even true.<br /> <br /> This programming is clearly seen in the Ananasi, but its quite strong in the Garou too. Their personality and their role in their society is set in the moment they born, by the moon. Even if that personality is brighter or darker, it's determined by the waxing or the wanning moon.<br /> <br /> The Garou are born with a mission. Comparing to them, a vampire who is Embraced, a mage who Awakens, a wraith that exits her caul, or even a Changelling that discovers his nature, all of them have to figure out and decide what to do with their lifes and how and with which purpose use their powers.<br /> <br /> So, are the Garou heroic? How could they be if they are programmed to do what they do. The few Garou that aren't &quot;heroic&quot; are those that were able to overcome that programming.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Their unnatural, because of their supernatural abilitys and the fact they cannot create healthy offspring with their own kind</b><br /> <br /> We have to admit she has a point. Every sexual animal can breed with their own. The mere sight of a Garou in its combat form breaks the mind of the humans that see them. When they get angry, or they feel so, they turn into a giant beast that kills and destroy everything. Why we have to accept that they are natural but vampire no, and mages neither (because they steal the powers that are not meant to them)?<br /> <br /> If Gaia created the Garou, it was God who created the vampires. He made them feed on blood and fear the sun, and everything they are.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>A bunch of bullshit about how Dogs have a definite evolutioinary advantage over wolves , how tool use IS an evolutionary advantage, and a bunch of other garbage.</b><br /> <br /> As said, dogs are wolves. And every specie in the world exits because ti had an evolutionary advantage. Of course, tool use is the ultimate evolutionary advantage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>oh some insanity about how environmentalism is the product of people who are not struggling to survive, and often considered gross hypocricy by those who are.</b><br /> <br /> Ok, I could not agree her here. Not looking after the environment is stupid and irresponsible. Even if I don't like this theme as a werewolf theme, polluting, wasting energy, etc. is destroying our own future.<br /> <br /> <b>ANOTHER peice of bullshit she had, was that lupus should be athiestic, since animals dont have religion....</b><br /> <br /> Lupus are religious because they are programmed to be so, they born with the certainity of that their religion is true.<br /> <br /> <b>Oh an argument that Garou are INFERIOR to humanity that I found really really sick.</b><br /> <br /> Well, I can argue because I don't know the argument, but I find interesting that you get sick to hear that your own kind is not superior to some monster.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>[mine] So, why are the Garou the villains of the show?</b><br /> <br /> You only have to look at the story. Before the scripture invention they initiated (by most records) a War of Rage in which they almost brought the other Changing Breeds to extintion. Then they cried in regret. Then, they arrived to America and started the second War of Rage, in which they almost extinguish the American Shapeshifters, destroyed the Camazotz, destroyed the Croatan, and reduced the number of the other native werewolf tribes. Then they cried again. And then they arrived to Australia, and started the War of Tears, and extinguished the Bunyip. As always, they cried after. Aren't they a cursed Breed?<br /> <br /> In the Beast Courts the only werewolves are those that in one way or another fight their nature. The Hakken do so via the human code of bushido. Still, they are xenophobic (they prefer to be in Hakken sentais) and warlike. The Stargazers have a long tradition of fighting their own rage, develop spiritually to overcome their nature and explore the way of inaction.<br /> <br /> If you want to claim the werewolves are heroes, you can ask their victims. Ask the Camazotz. Ask almost anyone, except the Garou.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3673-mu_","name":"Mu_","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3673_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T10:57:02-07:00","id":656735,"title":"","content":"Oh sorry to bump this thread after over a week lot happening, but 2 more pieces of BS One is that the umbra, is clearly just some alternate dimension given the fact that Hiroshima and Nagasaki both show as tainted in the umbral landscape in spite of having completely recovered in the physical world.<br /> <br /> the other was that the impergium was IMPOSSIBLE<br /> <br /> humans would have figured out how to create silver weapons, or absorbed silver into their blood, or made bargains with vampires and banes, or bargains with renegade garou, or some tribe would have bargained with humanity as partners and become the new dominant tribe, or some such bullshit.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T13:34:40-07:00","id":656861,"title":"","content":"The Umbra is a spiritual reflection of the Material World. So, you'll have strange things reflected into the Umbra that are not there in the Physical world. i.e. The Nukes dropped on Hiroshima and Nagasaksi left a spiritual scar that has not healed. The reflections in the Umbra also tend to be blown up in what they represent. An kinda creep alleyway in a City becomes a Nightmare inducing horror alley in the Umbra. A forest will become more foresty than it is in the Material World.<br /> <br /> The Impergium makes sense in Werewolf if Werewolf stands alone and the other splats are kinda vague. As in, Vampires and Mages and so on really aren't as much as a thing as they are in their own books. If you take into account a combined world, than the Impergium makes a lot less sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/1n0ov7p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3881-mental-mouse","name":"Mental-Mouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T13:37:24-07:00","id":656863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me?p=656735#post656735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh sorry to bump this thread after over a week lot happening, but 2 more pieces of BS One is that the umbra, is clearly just some alternate dimension given the fact that Hiroshima and Nagasaki both show as tainted in the umbral landscape in spite of having completely recovered in the physical world.</div> </div> </div> </div>The books are quite clear to the contrary. Sometimes people don't read them; it's like how someone I used to game with insisted that Gui Ren never die.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the other was that the impergium was IMPOSSIBLE<br /> <br /> humans would have figured out how to create silver weapons, </div> </div> </div>Urgh, that would be the start of things that would be annoying, if you were still talking to the party in question. Metalwork required an awful lot more infrastructure than humans had in prehistory, especially to refine silver to sterling-level purity or thereabouts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> or absorbed silver into their blood, </div> </div> </div>THE GAROU VULNERABILITY TO SILVER DOES NOT WORK THAT WAY! Besides, with the trace amounts in the environment and no capability to actually go beyond that, the levels of even biologically-bound silver, which would be a different thing from solid, elemental silver even when bound into a complex, wouldn't be high enough to matter. You'd know if they did; people would go beyond argyriosis and into being blue corpses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> or made bargains with vampires and banes, or bargains with renegade garou, or some tribe would have bargained with humanity as partners and become the new dominant tribe, or some such bullshit. </div> </div> </div>Garou managed to keep banes and other enemies a long way away (remember, as a coordinated whole, they defeated the Talons of the Wyrm), and vampires are quite relatively modern, occurring toward the end of the Impergium when Garou were deciding not to engage in it any more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T15:44:04-07:00","id":657046,"title":"","content":"I'm inclined to say that the Garou could probably have reinstitute the Impergium any time before the 19th century. Hell, they might be able to do it now. They would have no trouble killing off cave men who can't even smelt silver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T09:36:11-07:00","id":658033,"title":"","content":"Wow, your friend really thinks the Wrym would move out of such a massive place of destruction and desolation just because the humans rebuilt a few buildings? The Umbra <i>remembers</i> stuff dude. It'll take more than a century to wipe <i>that</i> shit clean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T12:42:54-07:00","id":663400,"title":"","content":"I don't agree completely with <b>Mu_</b>, but on the essentials, I think. I wouldn't say for sure that <b>Prince of the Night</b> needs to talk with her, because maybe she do hurts him. I don't know, I don't have the means to know.<br /> <br /> So lets stick to what can be known.<br /> <br /> The Umbra is a mess, actually. Very poorly defined in its whole. In the end, it is the entire phenomena of dimensional displacement. We can assume, though, that we're talking about its nearest layer from the Material perspective, what is <u>almost</u> well defined.<br /> <br /> Well, she's actually right! Hey, people, the Umbra IS an alternate dimension. And that is precisely why it didn't recovered as fast in Hiroshima and Nagasaki. Because it isn't the material plane, it is an alternate reality. What we do know and the book describes isn't that the Umbra is the same world, but that it is <b><u>linked</u></b> to the Material. So those rules about how one world affects and reflects the other aren't rules about one world working, but about two worlds interacting.<br /> <br /> And needing to interact, lets be clear about it. The Material and the Umbra are two, alternate, worlds. But they need each other. Like the gravity equilibrium in our solar system makes Earth dependent on every other planet, and to some degree respond to eventual changes on them, without being the same planet at all. In a sense, you could describe the relation between the Material and the Umbra as the relation between Earth and Moon and their gravity interaction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T01:49:04-08:00","id":1177202,"title":"","content":"Excerpt from Endgame, from chapter &quot;Apocalyse&quot;<br /> <br /> When a white man kills an Indian in a fair fight it is called honorable, but when an Indian kills a white man in a fair fight it is called murder. When a white army battles Indians and wins it is called a great victory, but if they lose it is called a massacre and bigger armies are raised. If the Indian flees before the advance of such armies, when he tries to return he finds that white men are living where he lived. If he tries to fight off such armies, he is killed and the land is taken anyway. When an Indian is killed, it is a great loss which leaves a gap in our people and a sorrow in our heart; when a white is killed three or four others step up to take his place and there is no end to it. The white man seeks to conquer nature, to bend it to his will and to use it wastefully until it is all gone and then he simply moves on, leaving the waste behind him and looking for new places to take. The whole white race is a monster who is always hungry and what he eats is land.<br /> <br /> Chiksika<br /> <br /> As a longtime grassroots environmental activist, and as a creature living in the thrashing endgame of civilization, I am intimately acquainted with the landscape of loss, and have grown accustomed to carrying the daily weight of despair. I have walked clearcuts that wrap around mountains, drop into valleys, then climb ridges to fragment watershed after watershed, and I\u2019ve sat silent near empty streams that two generations ago were \u201clashed into whiteness\u201d by uncountable salmon coming home to spawn and die.<br /> <br /> A few years ago I began to feel pretty apocalyptic. But I hesitated to use that word, in part because of those drawings I\u2019ve seen of crazy penitents carrying \u201cThe End is Near\u201d signs, and in part because of the power of the word itself. Apocalypse. I didn\u2019t want to use it lightly.<br /> <br /> But then a friend and fellow activist said, \u201cWhat will it take for you to finally call it an apocalypse? The death of the salmon? Global warming? The ozone hole? The reduction of krill populations off Antarctica by 90 percent, the turning of the sea off San Diego into a dead zone, the same for the Gulf of Mexico? How about the end of the great coral reefs? The extirpation of two hundred species per day? Four hundred? Six hundred? Give me a specific threshold, Derrick, a specific point at which you\u2019ll finally use that word.\u201d<br /> <br /> * * *<br /> <br /> Do you believe that our culture will undergo a voluntary transformation to a sane and sustainable way of living?<br /> <br /> For the last several years I\u2019ve taken to asking people this question, at talks and rallies, in libraries, on buses, in airplanes, at the grocery store, the hardware store. Everywhere. The answers range from emphatic nos to laughter. No one answers in the affirmative. One fellow at one talk did raise his hand, and when everyone looked at him, he dropped his hand, then said, sheepishly, \u201cOh, voluntary? No, of course not.\u201d My next question: how will this understanding\u2014that this culture will not voluntarily stop destroying the natural world, eliminating indigenous cultures, exploiting the poor, and killing those who resist\u2014shift our strategy and tactics? The answer? Nobody knows, because we never talk about it: we\u2019re too busy pretending the culture will undergo a magical transformation.<br /> <br /> This book is about that shift in strategy, and in tactics.<br /> <br /> * * *<br /> <br /> I just got home from talking to a new friend, another longtime activist. She told me of a campaign she participated in a few years ago to try to stop the government and transnational timber corporations from spraying Agent Orange, a potent defoliant and teratogen, in the forests of Oregon. Whenever activists learned a hillside was going to be sprayed, they assembled there, hoping their presence would stop the poisoning. But each time, like clockwork, helicopters appeared, and each time, like clockwork, helicopters dumped loads of Agent Orange onto the hillside and onto protesting activists. The campaign did not succeed.<br /> <br /> \u201cBut,\u201d she said to me, \u201cI\u2019ll tell you what did. A bunch of Vietnam vets lived in those hills, and they sent messages to the Bureau of Land Management and to Weyerhaeuser, Boise Cascade, and the other timber companies saying, \u2018We know the names of your helicopter pilots, and we know their addresses.\u2019\u201d<br /> <br /> I waited for her to finish.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou know what happened next?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cI think I do,\u201d I responded.<br /> <br /> \u201cExactly,\u201d she said. \u201cThe spraying stopped.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23713-aeg1sthus","name":"Aeg1sthus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23713_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T10:12:24-08:00","id":1177350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610887-beat-the-heroism-of-the-garou-back-into-me#post610887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I knew some ... jerk for a while who tried brainwashing me into thinking the garou arent heros.<br /> <br /> That environmentalism is garbage and some other bullshit.<br /> <br /> I submit myself for deprogramming</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThey're more like heroic bullies or jerks. You might find some of them unpleasant or obnoxious, but they help preserve &amp; save our natural environment. yet sometimes unfortunate mortals will get in the way &amp; accidently killed because of one or more pissed off Garou. So, it's hard for them to walk away from their more horrific aspects even if when you finally understand their noble cause. Kind of like that guy who destroyed the only space ship they had to shoot the Critter who was murdering them one by one. (From the fourth and last Critters film, in case your wondering.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent-lax3-1.xx.fbcdn.net/hphotos-xfl1/v/t1.0-9/11999058_1477906402511404_6367649438608181692_n.jpg?oh=70d49fe91b2932b397dc24c5df2764ba&amp;oe=56A3338B\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1056,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1056-wolf-man","user":"Wolf-Man","date":". 01-22-2018, 12:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1056-wolf-man","name":"Wolf-Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1056_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}